window.GEAR_BOOK_CONTENTS["book-32"] = [{"id":14,"rawContent":"# 第十四章：停屍房裡的第十三具冰櫃\n\n晚間八點四十分，暴雨如黑色瀑布般沖刷著濱江市公安局的防爆玻璃幕牆。\n\n警車的猩紅迴轉警燈在積水的院子裡劃出一道道刺目的光軌。涉案主犯秦墨被兩名全副武裝的特警押解下車，送往局裡最深處的重型審訊室。\n\n而在市局大樓地下一層的法醫病理實驗中心門口，老周終於換下了一身臭氣熏天的濕衣服，套著一件寬鬆的灰色警用抓絨衫，手裡依然緊緊攥著他那隻印著草莓圖案的粉紅色保溫杯。\n\n「小裴，我讓人去局裡食堂煮了兩碗薑湯麵，加了三個荷包蛋。」老周灌了一口熱茶，看著身旁提著銀色勘查箱的年輕人，「今晚算是把大劇院那一千八百多號人從鬼門關前拉回來了，楚天成那老狐狸也進了急救監護室，二十四小時有便衣看守。你說……秦墨被銬上時說的那句話，到底是什麼意思？」\n\n「秦墨在神經生理學與心理學上表現出典型的『從屬型反社會人格』。」裴以安刷開法醫中心的生物識別感應門，換上一次性防護服，「他具備頂級工匠的精微操作力，但思維架構嚴重依賴外部秩序。林清源死後三十年，他需要一個絕對強大的精神宿主來指揮他。那個真正的『擺渡人』，不僅掌握著三十年前的全部真相，更在幕後精準操控著秦墨的每一步行動。」\n\n自動玻璃門向兩側滑開，一股混合著福馬林、低溫冷氣與消毒水微酸味的空氣迎面撲來。\n\n對於裴以安而言，這種常人避之不及的氣味，卻是整座喧囂城市中最讓他感到寧靜與安全的氣息。\n\n「小李？今晚值班的李技術員呢？」老周走進解剖前室，按了按吧台上的呼叫鈴。\n\n前室空無一人，只有旋轉座椅在微風中輕輕搖晃，桌上放著半杯尚未喝完的速溶咖啡。\n\n「神經肌肉阻滯劑殘留氣味。」裴以安鼻翼微動，目光瞬間落在庫房角落的一張推車後方。\n\n只見年輕的李技術員正靠坐在牆角，雙眼緊閉，呼吸均勻綿長，脖頸處貼著一枚極微小的透明皮下滲透貼片。\n\n老周拔出腰間的警用電筒，立刻上前探查鼻息：「還有氣！脈搏平穩，跟大劇院那個首席小提琴家一樣，被精確麻醉了！」\n\n「這不是入侵，是宣告。」裴以安的聲音沒有一絲溫度。\n\n他徑直推開了通往最深處屍體冷藏庫的厚重氣密鉛門。\n\n「滋——滋——」\n\n就在兩人踏入冷藏庫的瞬間，頭頂上方的日光燈管突然發出一陣不祥的電弧爆鳴聲，整座地下室的照明猛然閃爍了兩下，隨後緊急備用發電機的暗紅色應急地燈幽幽亮起。\n\n在暗紅色的光影交錯中，冷藏庫內整齊排列的十二座不鏽鋼冷藏冰櫃宛如十二座冰冷的鋼鐵墓碑。\n\n然而，老周的目光越過常規的冰櫃矩陣，投向最內側的陰暗角落時，整個人猛地抽了一口涼氣。\n\n「小裴……你看那面牆……」\n\n冷藏庫原本平整的白瓷磚牆壁，此時竟被推開了一道半米寬的隱蔽暗門！\n\n那是一座深嵌在市局地下防空掩體水泥夾層內的冷藏空間。因為年代久遠、檔案交接缺失，就連在市局幹了三十年的老周，也從未見過這面暗牆後方的結構。\n\n而在暗門深處的冷氣繚繞之中，赫然延伸出一座獨立運轉的低溫冰櫃——\n\n那是冷藏庫裡的第十三具冰櫃！\n\n冰櫃的數位液晶溫控面板泛著冷冽的藍光，數字穩定在驚悚的「-18℃」。\n\n更令老周心驚肉跳的是，冰櫃的拉手上方，赫然掛著一張嶄新的黃銅證物吊牌，上面用工整的宋體鋼印壓印著一行編號：\n\n**【濱江市公安局·1994年特大溺亡疑案·專案編號94-0717】**\n\n**【死者：原市立醫院病理科主任——林清源】**\n\n「三十年前林博士的案卷……」老周的聲音顫抖得厲害，「當年林博士的遺體在二號乾塢打撈上來後，家屬簽字火化，骨灰早就下葬了……這第十三具冰櫃裡裝的又是誰？！」\n\n裴以安一言不發，戴上雙層乳膠手套與防護面罩，邁步走進暗室。\n\n他的手掌按在冰櫃那冰冷刺骨的純鋼把手上。\n\n「喀嗒。」\n\n隨著卡榫彈開的脆響，一股比常規冷藏庫濃烈數倍的乾冰白霧如瀑布般從櫃縫中洶湧湧出。\n\n裴以安雙臂發力，將重型不鏽鋼滑軌托盤緩緩向外拖出。\n\n當白霧在暗紅色應急燈下漸漸散去，托盤上的景象讓經驗豐富的老刑警倒退了半步，頭皮陣陣發麻——\n\n托盤上躺著的，不是一具乾枯的腐屍，也不是林清源缺失了頭骨的殘骸。\n\n那是一具身穿一九九四年標準版白色醫師大褂的人體全身骨架！\n\n骨架的兩百零六塊骨骼被極細的鈦合金鋼絲精密串聯，姿態優雅地仰臥在托盤中央。而在骨架的頸椎上方，原本安放頭骨的位置，此時卻空空如也，宛如在無聲地等待著下水道裡那顆頭骨的歸位。\n\n更詭異的是，在那具白骨雙手交疊的胸肋骨正中央，赫然端放著一台老式的微型磁帶錄音機！\n\n錄音機的磁帶倉敞開著，一盤泛黃的紅色卡帶靜靜卡在磁頭槽內。\n\n「老周，退後。」裴以安的聲音透著前所未有的凝重。\n\n他手持長柄鑷子，精準避開可能存在的重力機械觸發裝置，輕輕挑開了錄音機下方的襯墊。\n\n沒有炸藥，也沒有水銀開關。\n\n只有一張用醫用縫合線縫在醫師大褂胸口處的黑底金字卡片：\n\n*「敬愛的裴以安法醫：歡迎來到審判的核心。當你打開這具冰櫃時，死者的最後一場化驗便已進入倒計時。」*\n\n「滋——」\n\n就在裴以安看清字跡的同一微秒，冰櫃下方的微型機械繼電器突然自動咬合！\n\n那台沉睡了三十年的老式錄音機，磁帶軸輪竟毫無預兆地瘋狂旋轉起來！\n\n緊接著，冷藏庫原本敞開的重型氣密鉛門發出一聲震耳欲聾的鋼鐵碰撞巨響，沉重地自動鎖死！\n\n「砰——！！」\n\n頭頂的通風管道閥門瞬間逆轉，原本排出廢氣的通風口發出一陣尖銳的氣流倒灌聲。\n\n一股帶著淡淡杏仁苦味與微弱香草甜氣的無色氣體，如毒蛇般從通風孔中狂暴噴湧而出！\n\n老周撲向大門，瘋狂拉動緊急手動解鎖閥，但閥門早已被內部熔斷的保險絲死死卡死！\n\n「門被鎖死了！通風口在往裡灌氣！」老周猛拍著防爆玻璃，對著對講機大喊，但對講機裡只有一片刺耳的盲音雪花，「頻率被屏蔽了！小裴！這是什麼氣體？！」\n\n裴以安一把扯過兩具高規格防毒面罩，將其中一具重重扣在老周臉上，另一具迅速罩住自己的口鼻。\n\n金絲眼鏡後，裴以安的瞳孔縮成了兩枚冰冷的針尖，透過面罩的呼氣閥發出低沉而急促的警告：\n\n「高濃度七氟烷與惰性致冷氣溶膠。這是實驗室滅火與麻醉混合氣體，五分鐘內會排空室內氧氣並抑制中樞神經，造成窒息性昏迷。」\n\n裴以安猛然回頭，盯著第十三具冰櫃裡那具無頭骨架手中正在瘋狂轉動的磁帶：\n\n「擺渡人沒有坐在這裡等我們……這整座法醫中心，就是他為我們準備的解剖台！」","rawContentEn":"# Chapter 14: The Thirteenth Freezer in the Morgue\n\nAt 8:40 in the evening, torrential rain lashed against the reinforced glass curtain walls of the Binjiang Municipal Public Security Bureau like a dark waterfall.\n\nThe crimson flash of cruiser beacons traced piercing arcs across the flooded precinct courtyard. Escorted by two heavily armed SWAT officers, the primary suspect, Qin Mo, was marched from the transport van toward the maximum-security interrogation block.\n\nMeanwhile, outside the Forensic Pathology Laboratory on the building's subterranean first level, Old Zhou had finally peeled off his stench-ridden, sodden trousers. Now clad in a loose gray police fleece, he still clutched his pink thermal mug with its faded strawberry decal with unbroken devotion.\n\n\"Little Pei, I had the cafeteria whip up two piping-hot bowls of ginger noodle soup with three poached eggs,\" Old Zhou took a swig of warm tea, glancing sideways at the young man hoisting the silver field kit. \"Tonight we yanked more than eighteen hundred people back from the gates of hell. Old fox Chu Tiancheng is locked down under twenty-four-hour plainclothes surveillance in the ICU. But tell me... what did Qin Mo mean by that parting shot when the cuffs snapped shut?\"\n\n\"Qin Mo exhibits the classic psychophysiological profile of a subordinate antisocial personality,\" Pei Yi'an remarked, scanning his biometric badge at the laboratory portal and donning disposable protective coveralls. \"He commands the microscopic precision of a master horologist, yet his cognitive architecture relies desperately upon an external locus of control. Over the thirty years following Lin Qingyuan's demise, he required an omnipotent mental host to direct his actions. The true 'Ferryman' does not merely possess the full truth of 1994; he orchestrated every move Qin Mo executed tonight with mathematical precision.\"\n\nThe automated sliding glass doors parted, releasing an embrace of air infused with formalin, chilled refrigerant, and the faint, acidic bite of antiseptic wash.\n\nTo ordinary mortals, such a scent evoked dread; to Pei Yi'an, it was the purest, most tranquil sanctuary amidst the frantic noise of the living city.\n\n\"Technician Li? Where's the duty officer tonight?\" Old Zhou asked, stepping into the autopsy ante-room and rapping the call bell on the counter.\n\nThe reception area stood deserted. Only a swivel chair gently swayed in the draft, a half-finished mug of instant coffee cooling on the desk beside it.\n\n\"A trace signature of neuromuscular blockade agents,\" Pei Yi'an noted, his nostrils flaring slightly before his gaze snapped toward the corner behind a stainless gurney.\n\nSlumped against the corner wall sat young Technician Li, eyes closed, his breathing slow and rhythmic. Affixed to his jugular groove was an ultra-thin transdermal micro-patch.\n\nUnsheathing his flashlight, Old Zhou bounded forward to check the technician's airway: \"He's alive! Vitals are steady. Same as that guest violinist at the Grand Theatre—titrated down to the microgram!\"\n\n\"This is not an intrusion; it is a proclamation,\" Pei Yi'an said, his voice void of warmth.\n\nHe strode straight toward the heavy lead-shielded airtight door that guarded the inner mortuary vault.\n\n*Zzzzt—zzzzt—*\n\nThe instant their boots crossed the threshold, the overhead fluorescent luminaires hummed with an ominous electric arc. The subterranean chamber's lighting blinked twice in rapid succession before succumbing to the dull, bloody glow of auxiliary emergency baseboard runners.\n\nAmidst the crimson gloom, the twelve stainless-steel mortuary drawers stood arrayed like twelve silent, glacial tombstones.\n\nYet as Old Zhou's gaze scanned beyond the standard freezer bay toward the shadowed recesses, all air fled his lungs in a ragged gasp.\n\n\"Little Pei... look at that partition wall...\"\n\nIn the seamless expanse of ceramic tiles, a half-meter gap had slid quietly open into a hidden crypt!\n\nIt was a concealed refrigeration annex embedded deep within the reinforced concrete sandwich of the municipal bomb shelter. Obscured by decades and lost administrative handovers, even Old Zhou, with thirty years on the force, had never glimpsed the space behind that wall.\n\nAnd deep within the swirling fog behind that secret door extended a lone, humming low-temperature vault—\n\nIt was the thirteenth freezer in the morgue!\n\nIts digital LED readout glowed with an icy cyan light, hovering steadily at a chilling \"-18°C.\"\n\nWhat made Old Zhou's pulse race even faster was the pristine brass evidence tag dangling from the central pull-latch, crisply stamped in block typeface:\n\n**[Binjiang Municipal Public Security Bureau · 1994 Suspicious Drowning Cold Case · Docket No. 94-0717]**\n\n**[Deceased: Former Chief of Pathology, Municipal Hospital—Dr. Lin Qingyuan]**\n\n\"Dr. Lin's cold case file from thirty years ago...\" Old Zhou's voice shook with uncharacteristic tremor. \"Back then, when Dr. Lin's remains were pulled from Dry Dock No. 2, the family signed the cremation waiver and his ashes were interred decades ago... Just who on earth is sealed inside this thirteenth freezer?!\"\n\nPei Yi'an uttered not a syllable. Donning double latex gloves and a sterile face shield, he stepped calmly into the hidden recess.\n\nHis fingers clamped around the bone-chilling steel handle of the drawer.\n\n*Click.*\n\nWith the sharp release of the spring catch, a dense cascade of sub-zero dry-ice vapor billowed outward like a miniature cataract.\n\nEngaging his forearms, Pei Yi'an steadily drew the heavy stainless-steel rolling tray out along its lubricated runners.\n\nAs the fog parted under the crimson emergency glow, the spectacle resting upon the slab forced even the hardened veteran detective half a step back, his scalp prickling with sheer cold dread—\n\nWhat lay upon the tray was neither a desiccated cadaver nor Lin Qingyuan's headless skeleton.\n\nIt was an intact, articulated adult human skeleton, dressed impeccably in a vintage 1994 regulation white physician's lab coat!\n\nAll two hundred and six bones had been strung together with microscopic titanium wire, reposing with serene elegance in the center of the tray. Above the first cervical vertebra, where the skull should have rested, sat an empty cradle—as if waiting in silent expectation for the cranium recovered from the conduit to be returned.\n\nOdder still, nestled directly between the crossed skeletal forearms over the sternum rested an antique micro-cassette tape recorder!\n\nThe cassette bay gaped open, an aged red tape cartridge sitting poised beneath the magnetic read head.\n\n\"Old Zhou, step back,\" Pei Yi'an commanded, his voice weighted with rare gravity.\n\nArmed with long-shank forceps, he cautiously probed the padding beneath the recorder, deftly steering clear of any potential mechanical tripwires.\n\nThere were no explosive bricks, nor mercury level-switches.\n\nOnly a gilded black card sewn into the coat's breast pocket with surgical braided silk:\n\n*\"Dear Pathologist Pei Yi'an: Welcome to the nucleus of judgment. The instant you unsealed this freezer, the final post-mortem of the departed commenced its countdown.\"*\n\n*Zzzzz—*\n\nThe very microsecond Pei Yi'an parsed the final syllable, a micro-solenoid beneath the tray snapped shut!\n\nInside the thirty-year-old tape recorder, the capstans spun into frantic, humming life!\n\nIn the next heartbeat, the open lead-lined hermetic portal of the morgue slammed shut with a concussive metallic crash, deadbolts driving deep into the jamb!\n\n*SLAM—!!*\n\nOverhead, the damper actuators of the HVAC ducts reversed violently, the exhaust grates whistling with high-pressure backdraft.\n\nA colorless aerosol carrying the bitter hint of almonds and a subtle trace of synthetic vanilla spewed violently into the vault like an invisible serpent!\n\nOld Zhou hurled himself against the slab, wrenching desperately at the manual bypass lever, only to find the cam-locks welded fast by blown thermal fuses!\n\n\"The door is sealed! The vents are pumping poison in!\" Old Zhou slammed his fists on the armored glass, shouting into his radio only to meet deafening white noise. \"Signal's jammed! Little Pei! What kind of gas is this?!\"\n\nPei Yi'an tore down two high-grade NBC respirators from the emergency locker, shoving one over Old Zhou's head before strapping the second firmly over his own visage.\n\nBehind his gold frames, Pei Yi'an's pupils shrunk into twin icy needle-points as his voice rasped through the exhale valve:\n\n\"High-concentration sevoflurane blended with inert halon aerosol. It is an industrial laboratory fire-suppressant and anesthetic compound—within five minutes, it will displace all ambient oxygen and depress the central nervous system into an asphyxiant coma.\"\n\nPei Yi'an whirled toward the spinning cassette nestled between the skeletal hands of the thirteenth freezer:\n\n\"The Ferryman never intended to sit here awaiting our arrival... This entire Forensic Pathology Center is the operating theater he prepared for our dissection!\""},{"id":15,"rawContent":"# 第十五章：低溫冰櫃與密室呼吸\n\n防毒面罩的橡膠邊緣緊緊壓迫著面部神經，傳來粗重而規律的呼吸聲。\n\n透過面罩的聚碳酸酯透鏡，冷藏庫內的世界被應急地燈染成一片壓抑的血紅色。高濃度的七氟烷與惰性致冷氣溶膠如同一層冰冷的薄紗，在半空中緩緩盤旋沉降。\n\n「小裴……這面罩的濾毒罐……能撐多久？」老周背靠著緊閉的氣密鉛門，右手死死攥著警槍，左手依然條件反射般護在胸前的粉紅色保溫杯上。他的聲音透過面罩的單向呼氣閥傳出，沉悶得猶如隔著一層厚重的棉絮。\n\n「常規防毒濾罐在這種工業級濃度的氣溶膠環境下，有效防護時間最多只有十二分鐘。」裴以安抬起手腕看了一眼機械錶的夜光指針，聲音冷靜得沒有半點情緒起伏，「十二分鐘後，濾毒碳層飽和穿透，我們會在兩分鐘內陷入深度麻醉與缺氧性休克。」\n\n「他娘的，老子辦了一輩子案子，最後要是死在自家單位的停屍房裡，傳出去得讓隔壁刑偵支隊笑上三十年！」老周狠狠咬著牙，目光投向門口已被熔斷的電子鎖面板，「剛才對講機已經徹底成了啞巴，地下室的信號被全頻段干擾了。老陸他們在地面上就算發現不對勁，要調防暴工兵組來切開這扇三十公分厚的防空鉛門，起碼得半個小時！」\n\n「擺渡人不會給我們半個小時。」裴以安轉過身，目光重新落在第十三具冰櫃托盤上的那具白骨身上。\n\n就在此時，那台被無頭骨架雙手捧在胸前的老式微型磁帶錄音機，揚聲孔中突然傳出了一陣粗糙刺耳的電流沙沙聲。\n\n緊接著，一道經過調音器精密過濾、分不清男女老幼的電子變聲，在死寂的冷藏庫內緩緩響起：\n\n『晚上好，裴以安法醫，還有周成林警官。』\n\n那聲音極為平和，甚至帶著一種優雅的學術探討意味：\n\n『三十年前，林清源博士試圖將整個濱江市最大的醫藥黑幕封存在這座防空地堡裡。但他太相信體制，太相信活人的道德，最終被權力與金屬錘擊碎了頭骨。』\n\n老周的眼角劇烈抽搐了一下，握槍的手指因用力過度而泛白。\n\n『今晚，你們兩位用手術刀與微調電路證明了自己的智慧。但正義不是廉價的掌聲，它需要用死者的邏輯來交換。』錄音機裡的聲音頓了頓，帶著一絲冷酷的笑意，『這座冷藏庫的氣密鎖採用了冷戰時期的純機械氣壓聯鎖裝置，暴力破拆只會觸發備用充氮閥，將室內氧氣在十秒內徹底抽空。唯一的解鎖密碼，就刻在你們面前這具遺骨的身上。』\n\n『你們還有最後十分鐘，證明你們配得上繼承林清源的解剖刀。』\n\n「啪嗒。」\n\n錄音機的磁帶軸輪驟然停轉，暗紅色的庫房再次陷入了令人窒息的死寂。\n\n「刻在骨頭上？！」老周一步跨上前，拿著強光電筒就要去翻動托盤上的肋骨，「小裴，快看！哪根骨頭有字？！」\n\n「不要用手碰。」裴以安冷聲喝止，長臂一展將老周擋在身後，「這具骨架兩百零六塊骨骼均經過微米級鋼絲懸吊配重，底部托盤連接著重力微動開關。任何非解剖學規範的外力牽拉，都會被判定為無效操作。」\n\n裴以安深吸了一口氣，強迫自己的呼吸保持絕對勻速，以節約寶貴的罐內氧氣。\n\n他拉開銀色勘查箱，取出一柄高精度的鈦合金骨科探針與便攜式多波段法醫光源。\n\n紫藍色的冷光如水銀瀉地般灑在整具白骨之上。在四百五十納米波長的照射下，骨骼表面原本肉眼不可見的細微痕跡頓時泛起一抹幽綠的熒光。\n\n「這具骨架……根本不是林清源。」裴以安俯下身，鼻尖距離第四胸椎僅有五公分，長探針精準地點在右側橈骨與尺骨的遠端關節處。\n\n「不是林博士？！」老周愣住了，「那他是誰？」\n\n「你看橈骨遠端的松質骨修復痕跡。」裴以安用探針輕輕敲擊骨質表面，傳來微弱清脆的金屬撞擊聲，「這裡植入了一枚長一點五公分的醫用純鈦接骨螺釘，採用的是瑞士第一代非自攻螺紋工藝。而左側鎖骨有嚴重的陳舊性骨折畸形癒合，鎖骨下動脈溝有明顯的骨贅壓迫增生——這是長期單肩背負重型測繪儀器造成的典型職業形變。」\n\n老周的腦海中轟然炸開了一道驚雷：「三十年前……跟在林清源身邊負責地下工程測繪的那個年輕工兵……陳默的親生父親？！」\n\n「陳衛國，一九九四年濱江市政地下工程首席測繪師。」裴以安的聲音沒有一絲波瀾，手中的紫光燈迅速下移，落在骨架的第七胸椎與胸骨柄的交界處，「林清源遇害前三天，陳衛國在防空掩體地下管網檢修中遭遇『瓦斯爆燃』殉職。官方檔案記錄他的遺體已被完全碳化，但實際上……他的遺骨被秘密製成了防空地堡的永久生物坐標。」\n\n「擺渡人把他藏在這裡整整三十年……」老周的眼眶泛紅，嘴唇在面罩後劇烈發抖，「他到底要我們找什麼？！」\n\n「解鎖機構不在門上，而在排水閥底座。」裴以安的探針順著第七肋骨下方那根極細的銀絲向下延伸，直接指向了第十三具冰櫃托盤最底部的排污漏斗。\n\n在那座純鋼鑄造的排污漏斗中央，赫然鑲嵌著一具老式的機械天平砝碼盤！\n\n砝碼盤的邊緣刻著一行用德語蝕刻的警示標籤：**【 Ausgleichsgewicht : 450 Gramm 】**。\n\n「四百五十克……」老周盯著那個天平盤，「這是什麼意思？要我們在停屍房裡找一塊四百五十克的砝碼？！」\n\n「四百五十克，正是成年男性心臟在生理鹽水充盈狀態下的標準重量。」裴以安眼中閃過一抹洞悉一切的銳芒，「三十年前的設計者將這座地堡的最後生還通道，設計成了『心臟的祭品』。只要砝碼盤感受到精確到克的下壓力，底部的氣動閥就會反向排氣，頂開安全門栓。」\n\n「可是這鬼地方除了骨頭就是福馬林，上哪兒去找剛好四百五十克的東西？！」老周急得直跺腳，防毒面罩內的呼吸指針已經開始劇烈偏向警戒紅區。\n\n裴以安緩緩轉過頭，金絲眼鏡後的目光平靜地落在老周懷裡。\n\n更準確地說，是落在他懷裡那隻粉紅色的保溫杯上。\n\n老周順著他的目光低頭看了一眼，整個人像被蠍子蜇了一樣往後縮了半步：「小裴！你……你小子該不會是要打老子保溫杯的主意吧？！這杯子我用了八年！裡面裝的是局裡特供的大紅袍！」\n\n「雙層不鏽鋼真空結構，空杯重量兩百一十克。」裴以安語速飛快，精準報出一連串數據，「八點四十分出發前，你在食堂飲水機接了半杯溫水，按照水位線估算，杯內水體約為兩百四十毫升，即兩百四十克。兩者相加，總重量恰好為四百五十克，誤差不超過一點五克。」\n\n「真……真的假的？」老周瞪大了眼睛。\n\n「周隊，我們還有最後兩分鐘。」裴以安伸出手，語氣不容置疑，「要麼交出保溫杯，要麼五分鐘後我們的心臟被當作真正的四百五十克砝碼切下來。」\n\n老周咬緊牙關，臉上的橫肉狠狠抽搐了兩下，終於無比肉痛地將那隻粉紅色的保溫杯遞到了裴以安手中：「輕點！千萬別給老子磕了！」\n\n裴以安接過保溫杯，動作穩健得如同在進行一場心臟搭橋手術。\n\n他屏住呼吸，雙手捧著保溫杯，極其平穩地將杯底懸停在排污漏斗的天平盤正上方一毫米處。\n\n三、二、一。\n\n手指鬆開。\n\n「喀嗒。」\n\n粉紅色的保溫杯穩穩落在不鏽鋼砝碼盤正中央！\n\n天平指針向下沉降了精準的三毫米，緊接著，冰櫃底座下方傳來了一陣機油潤滑的齒輪咬合聲！\n\n「哧————！！」\n\n一股強勁的高壓氣流猛然從排污管底部的旁路噴湧而出，將冷藏庫內積聚的白霧與麻醉氣溶膠瞬間抽向地底深處！\n\n緊接著，那扇厚重無比的氣密鉛門傳來了一聲沉悶的解鎖巨響！\n\n「咔嚓！」\n\n重達數百公斤的鋼鐵門栓在氣動頂針的推動下向外彈開，外側走廊明亮清新的空氣順著門縫狂湧而入！\n\n老周一把扯掉臉上的防毒面罩，大口大口地呼吸著清涼的空氣，整個人差點虛脫在門邊。他抹了一把額頭的冷汗，第一反應卻是撲回去將自己的保溫杯抱進懷裡，仔細檢查了一圈發現毫髮無損，才長長舒了一口氣。\n\n「他娘的……老子這隻保溫杯，今天算是立了一等功！」老周喘著粗氣，咧嘴露出一抹劫後餘生的笑容。\n\n然而，裴以安卻沒有笑。\n\n他站在第七胸椎骨旁，手中的銀色長鑷子正從骨架肋骨內側的縫隙中，夾出了一枚只有米粒大小、被微型塑料套管密封著的微型晶片。\n\n錄音機那沉寂的喇叭裡，突然跳過了磁帶接縫，傳來了擺渡人最後的低語：\n\n『做得很好，裴法醫。你比三十年前那些偽造檢驗單的庸醫，更配得上聆聽死者的低語。』\n\n『帶上陳衛國肋骨上的坐標，去市局檔案大樓的頂層天台吧。三十年前那場大火的真正點火人，正在那裡等著你們送去最後的起訴書。』\n\n裴以安收起鑷子，將微型晶片小心翼翼地放入證物管。\n\n他轉過身，金絲眼鏡後的那雙眼眸冷冽如初冬的薄冰，望向通往檔案大樓的走廊盡頭：\n\n「老周，喝口熱茶。我們的最後一具解剖台，在天台上。」","rawContentEn":"# Chapter 15: Cryogenic Vault and Confined Respiration\n\nThe rubber seal of the gas mask pressed hard against facial nerves, echoing with heavy, disciplined respiration.\n\nThrough the polycarbonate lenses of the respirators, the mortuary vault was bathed in an oppressive crimson glow cast by emergency floor lamps. High-concentration sevoflurane and inert refrigerant aerosols hovered like a chilling veil, swirling slowly before settling across the room.\n\n\"Little Pei... these filter canisters... how long can they last?\" Old Zhou leaned his back against the sealed hermetic lead door, his right hand gripping his service pistol, his left instinctively shielding the pink thermos tucked against his chest. His voice muffled through the one-way exhalation valve, sounding as if stifled behind thick wadding.\n\n\"Under an aerosol environment of this industrial concentration, standard activated carbon canisters provide at most twelve minutes of effective filtration,\" Pei Yi'an glanced at the luminous dial of his mechanical wristwatch, his voice smooth and devoid of emotional flutter. \"After twelve minutes, the carbon beds will saturate and rupture; within two minutes thereafter, we will succumb to profound surgical anesthesia and hypoxic shock.\"\n\n\"Damn it all! I've cracked homicides my whole life—if I end up suffocating in my own department's morgue, the neighboring precincts will laugh at my ghost for thirty years!\" Old Zhou gritted his teeth, glaring at the melted keypad panel by the portal. \"Our radios went completely dead; the subterranean band is jammed solid. Even if Chief Lu upstairs suspects foul play, rallying the breaching team to cut through thirty centimeters of armored lead will take at least half an hour!\"\n\n\"The Ferryman will not grant us half an hour,\" Pei Yi'an pivoted, his gaze settling anew on the skeletal remains resting upon the tray of the thirteenth freezer.\n\nAt that precise instant, the grille of the vintage micro-cassette recorder cradled across the headless skeleton's chest crackled with a burst of static.\n\nImmediately thereafter, an electronically modulated voice—its pitch synthesized to erase age and gender—resonated with chilling serenity through the dead vault:\n\n\"Good evening, Pathologist Pei Yi'an, and Detective Zhou Chenglin.\"\n\nThe timbre was unnervingly measured, carrying the polite cadence of an academic discourse:\n\n\"Thirty years ago, Dr. Lin Qingyuan sought to seal the greatest pharmaceutical conspiracy in Binjiang within this underground bomb shelter. Yet he placed too much faith in institutions, too much faith in the morality of the living, and ultimately paid with his cranium shattered under the weight of metal and power.\"\n\nA muscle near Old Zhou's eyelid twitched violently, his knuckles whitening around his sidearm.\n\n\"Tonight, you two demonstrated sharp intellect with scalpels and resonant frequencies. But justice is no cheap applause; it demands transaction through the logic of the departed.\" The voice paused, tinged with a razor-thin chuckle. \"The hermetic seals of this chamber utilize Cold War mechanical pneumatic linkages. Any forced breaching will merely trip the auxiliary nitrogen flush, purging all remaining oxygen within ten seconds. The sole bypass cipher is etched upon the skeleton before you.\"\n\n\"You have ten minutes remaining to prove yourselves worthy of inheriting Lin Qingyuan's dissecting blade.\"\n\nClick.\n\nThe recorder's capstans abruptly locked into stillness, plunging the crimson-lit room back into suffocating silence.\n\n\"Etched onto the bones?!\" Old Zhou bolted forward, brandishing his tactical torch to inspect the ribcage on the tray. \"Little Pei, look! Which bone has the inscription?!\"\n\n\"Do not touch it with bare hands,\" Pei Yi'an barked coldly, sweeping an arm outward to bar Old Zhou's advance. \"All two hundred and six bones in this frame are suspended by micro-metric wires calibrated to precise counterweights, connected directly to micro-switches beneath the tray. Any non-anatomical traction will be treated as tampering.\"\n\nPei Yi'an drew a measured breath, forcing his lungs into steady cadences to husband the dwindling oxygen inside his canister.\n\nHe unlatched his silver field kit, withdrawing a high-precision titanium orthopedic probe and a multi-wavelength forensic light source.\n\nCold violet-blue beams washed across the pristine skeleton. Under the 450-nanometer excitation wavelength, subtle micro-striations invisible to the naked eye fluoresced with an eerie, emerald radiance.\n\n\"This skeleton... is not Lin Qingyuan,\" Pei Yi'an bent down, his visor hovering barely five centimeters from the fourth thoracic vertebra as his probe tapped the distal radio-ulnar junction.\n\n\"Not Dr. Lin?!\" Old Zhou froze. \"Then who is this?\"\n\n\"Examine the trabecular remodeling on the distal radius,\" Pei Yi'an tapped the osseous surface, eliciting a faint, distinct metallic chime. \"An internal fixation screw—1.5-centimeter medical-grade titanium, utilizing Swiss first-generation non-self-tapping threads. Furthermore, the left clavicle shows malunion of an old fracture with prominent osteophyte proliferation along the subclavian groove—a textbook occupational deformity resulting from carrying heavy geodetic theodolites on a single shoulder.\"\n\nA thunderclap detonated in Old Zhou's memory: \"Thirty years ago... the young sapper who handled subterranean mapping alongside Dr. Lin... Chen Mo's biological father?!\"\n\n\"Chen Weiguo, chief surveyor of Binjiang's municipal underground conduits in 1994,\" Pei Yi'an said flatly, tracing the UV beam down to the junction of the seventh thoracic vertebra and the sternum. \"Three days prior to Lin Qingyuan's murder, Chen Weiguo supposedly perished in a 'gas explosion' during a tunnel inspection. Official records stated his remains were reduced to ash. In reality... his skeleton was preserved as a permanent biological coordinate within this shelter.\"\n\n\"The Ferryman kept him hidden here for thirty entire years...\" Old Zhou's eyes reddened, his lips quivering behind the visor. \"What exactly does he want us to find?!\"\n\n\"The bypass mechanism is not on the door; it is in the drainage sump,\" Pei Yi'an traced the silver filament dangling beneath the seventh rib downward, terminating at the stainless discharge funnel under the rolling tray.\n\nSet squarely in the center of that cast-steel drainage funnel was a mechanical balance pan!\n\nEngraved along the beveled brass rim was an etched German inscription: **【 Ausgleichsgewicht : 450 Gramm 】**.\n\n\"Four hundred and fifty grams...\" Old Zhou squinted at the counterpan. \"What does that mean? Are we supposed to scavenge a 450-gram balance weight in a morgue?!\"\n\n\"Four hundred and fifty grams represents the physiological standard weight of an adult male heart infused with saline,\" Pei Yi'an's eyes glinted with razor-sharp insight. \"Thirty years ago, the architect designed the escape conduit of this vault as an 'offering of the heart.' The moment the pan registers downward force calibrated to the exact gram, the pneumatic valve vents in reverse, unlatching the deadbolts.\"\n\n\"But in this godforsaken place, all we have are bones and formalin! Where the devil do we find something weighing exactly 450 grams?!\" Old Zhou stomped in frantic desperation, the pressure needle on his canister gauge twitching toward the red zone.\n\nPei Yi'an turned his head in measured stillness, his spectacles fixing upon Old Zhou's chest.\n\nMore specifically, upon the pink thermos clasped protectively in Old Zhou's arms.\n\nTracking his gaze downward, Old Zhou shrank back half a step as if stung: \"Little Pei! You... you aren't eyeing my thermos, are you?! I've carried this cup for eight years! It's brewing top-grade Da Hong Pao tea from the bureau canteen!\"\n\n\"Dual-layer vacuum stainless construction—tare weight 210 grams,\" Pei Yi'an rattled off figures with computational speed. \"Prior to departing at 8:40, you filled it halfway from the canteen dispenser; judging by the thermal fill line, the volume sits at roughly 240 milliliters, or 240 grams. Summed together, total mass is precisely 450 grams, with a margin of error under 1.5 grams.\"\n\n\"Are... are you pulling my leg?\" Old Zhou's eyes widened behind his visor.\n\n\"Captain Zhou, we have two minutes left,\" Pei Yi'an extended an open palm, his tone leaving zero room for debate. \"Hand over the thermos, or in five minutes our literal hearts will be excised to serve as the 450-gram balance.\"\n\nClenching his jaw as his facial muscles twitched, Old Zhou relinquished his beloved pink flask with immense heartache: \"Gentle! Don't you dare scratch the paint!\"\n\nPei Yi'an took the mug, his movements as steady as a cardiovascular surgeon executing a coronary bypass.\n\nHolding his breath, he cupped the flask with both hands, hovering its base one millimeter above the center of the balance pan.\n\nThree. Two. One.\n\nFingers released.\n\nClack.\n\nThe pink thermos settled dead-center onto the stainless steel plate!\n\nThe pointer depressed by precisely three millimeters; an instant later, lubricated gear trains hummed beneath the chassis!\n\nSHHHHHH—!!\n\nA ferocious exhaust surge roared through the drainage bypass, vacuuming the swirling mist and anesthetic aerosol down into the deep earth!\n\nNext came a resounding thud of disengaging cams from the massive lead door!\n\nCLANG!\n\nDriven by pneumatic pistons, the hundred-kilogram locking pins snapped free, allowing crisp, cool corridor air to rush into the chamber!\n\nOld Zhou tore off his mask, gulping down greedy lungs of fresh air as he slumped against the doorframe. Wiping cold sweat from his brow, his very first impulse was to lunge back and scoop his thermos into his embrace, sighing with profound relief after verifying it was unblemished.\n\n\"Damn it... this mug of mine deserves a First-Class Citation of Merit today!\" Old Zhou wheezed, breaking into a haggard grin.\n\nPei Yi'an, however, showed no amusement.\n\nStanding beside the seventh thoracic vertebra, his silver forceps deftly extracted a rice-grain-sized microchip sheathed in sealed silicone from between the ribs.\n\nFrom the tape player's speaker, past the spliced leader tape, drifted the Ferryman's final whisper:\n\n\"Excellently done, Doctor Pei. You are far more worthy of hearing the dead whisper than the quacks who falsified autopsies thirty years ago.\"\n\n\"Take the coordinates cached in Chen Weiguo's ribs and proceed to the rooftop of the Archives Building. The true arsonist who lit the blaze thirty years ago awaits your indictment there.\"\n\nRetracting his tweezers, Pei Yi'an slipped the microchip into a sterile cryovial.\n\nHe turned, his gaze behind his gold frames as sharp as early winter ice as he stared down the subterranean corridor toward the archives tower:\n\n\"Old Zhou, drink your warm tea. Our final autopsy table awaits on the roof.\""},{"id":16,"rawContent":"# 第十六章：檔案大樓天台的雨夜終局\n\n狂暴的江風裹挾著冰冷的雨點，如刀子般抽打在市局舊檔案大樓十二層的天台鐵門上。\n\n晚間九點十五分。\n\n這座修建於一九八二年的灰磚檔案樓早已列入拆遷序列，整座大樓的電梯早在五年前便已停運，空氣中瀰漫著濃重的潮濕紙漿霉味與陳年混凝土的粉塵氣息。\n\n老周手持強光戰術手電筒，氣喘吁吁地推開了通往天台的最後一道生鏽鐵門，腳下的防暴軍靴在積水泛黃的水門汀地面上踏出急促的水花。\n\n「小裴……慢點！老子這條老腿……今天爬了一百八十級台階，半月板都要磨平了！」老周抹了一把臉上的雨水，另一手依然死死把那隻立了大功的粉紅色保溫杯護在抓絨衣口袋裡，「你確定陳衛國肋骨上的坐標，指的是這座破檔案樓的避雷針基座？」\n\n「微型晶片採用的是早期軍用甚高頻射頻識別技術，感應半徑不超過五十米。」裴以安快步穿過天台門檻，風衣在狂風中劇烈鼓動。他手中的便攜式頻譜儀螢幕上，一個猩紅的坐標點正以每秒兩次的頻率劇烈閃爍，與前方的避雷針鐵塔精準重合。\n\n閃電撕裂低垂的鉛雲，慘白的電光將天台中央照得一片雪亮。\n\n在天台邊緣那座高聳的角鋼通訊鐵塔下，一道瘦削修長的身影正靜靜背對著兩人，佇立在雨幕的最深處。\n\n那人身上披著一件寬大的黑色防雨風衣，狂風將他的衣擺撕扯得獵獵作響。他的身形微微佝僂，左肩明顯高於右肩，右手拄著一根通體由碳纖維與純鈦打造的醫用拐杖。\n\n而在他的腳邊，端放著一隻早已停產的八十年代牛皮公文包，包面上用燙金鋼印刻著一行磨損嚴重的字樣：**【濱江市公安局·刑事技術科·法醫專用】**。\n\n「三十年了，老周，你爬樓梯喘粗氣的毛病，還是一點都沒變。」\n\n一道沙啞、蒼老，卻又透著無比熟悉的溫和嗓音，穿透狂風與暴雨的呼嘯，緩緩飄進老周的耳中。\n\n老周的身軀猛地僵死在原地，手中的強光手電筒險些脫手墜落。\n\n「這聲音……」老周的瞳孔驟然放大，聲音因極度的震驚與駭然變了調，「老顧？！顧志明？！怎麼可能是你？！」\n\n拄著鈦合金拐杖的身影緩緩轉過身來。\n\n慘白的電光照亮了他的面容——那是一張布滿深深刻痕的消瘦面孔，雙鬢斑白如霜，鼻樑上架著一副與裴以安極為相似的無框金絲眼鏡。\n\n顧志明，前任市局法醫病理科主任，老周三十年前初入刑偵隊時的帶教搭檔，更是裴以安七年前進入司法部法醫研究所時的引薦導師！\n\n他在三年前因嚴重的骨髓增生異常綜合徵宣布因病退休，此後便消失在公眾視野中。\n\n「顧老師。」裴以安停下腳步，神色依舊清冷如雪，但垂在身側的手指卻微不可察地收緊了一下，「從大劇院那把骨弓上的雙軸游絲微調卡榫，到第十三具冰櫃裡那具陳衛國的全身骨架……所有的防腐處理技術與微米級解剖手法，都是您三十年前發表的博士論文專利。」\n\n「小裴，你是我教過最優秀的學生，甚至超越了當年的我和林清源。」顧志明抬手摘下被雨水打濕的眼鏡，用一塊乾燥的鹿皮布平靜地擦拭著鏡片，「死者不會說謊，骨骼記錄了一切。這句話，是我第一天把你帶進解剖室時教給你的。」\n\n「那你為什麼要當『擺渡人』？！」老周紅著眼眶咆哮，大步衝上前，槍口在顫抖中指向自己昔日的摯友，「三十年前林博士遇害，檢驗報告上的簽字是你！說林博士是『失足溺水』的也是你！你拿著楚天成的封口費步步高升，三十年後你居然還有臉用這些骨頭來搞連環私刑？！」\n\n「老周，你以為我是為了升官發財？」顧志明嘴角泛起一抹淒涼而自嘲的慘笑，他緩緩解開了防雨風衣的排扣。\n\n在深藍色的襯衫下方，赫然露出了一具緊緊包裹著他整個胸椎與腰椎的醫用鈦合金外固定支架。\n\n「看這裡，小裴，給你的老師做一場生前切片。」顧志明指著自己畸形隆起的脊柱，聲音平靜得像在講解一具教學標本。\n\n裴以安上前一步，目光落在顧志明胸椎第七節至腰椎第二節的X光投影外固定板上。\n\n「胸腰段骨質瀰漫性溶骨性破壞，骨皮質呈穿鑿樣缺損，伴有嚴重的病理性壓縮性骨折。」裴以安吐出冰冷的診斷名詞，「多發性骨髓瘤晚期，骨轉移灶已經侵蝕了神經根。您最多只剩下三個月的生命。」\n\n「沒錯，三個月。」顧志明重新戴上眼鏡，雨水順著他的鏡片蜿蜒滑落，「三十年前，楚天成帶著省廳副廳長的調令走進我的解剖室，把一把純銅手術錘砸在林清源的屍體旁。他威脅我，如果我不簽下溺亡報告，我剛剛出生的女兒就會在保溫箱裡『因醫療事故窒息』。」\n\n老周握槍的手猛烈一顫，臉上的肌肉痛苦地扭曲起來。\n\n「我妥協了，我簽了字，我當了三十年的懦夫與幫兇！」顧志明枯瘦的手指死死扣住拐杖把手，青筋暴凸，「林清源是我的摯友，陳衛國是為了替他取證而死。這三十年來，每一塊被楚天成吞併的專利，都在我的骨髓裡化成了癌細胞！我的骨頭每一分每一秒都在痛，那是林清源和陳衛國在向我索命！」\n\n「所以你找到了流亡的秦墨，收他為徒，策劃了這場跨越三十年的審判？」裴以安問。\n\n「秦墨是手術刀，而我是繪製解剖圖的人。」顧志明彎下腰，將腳邊的那隻牛皮公文包緩緩提起，遞向裴以安，「楚天成以為三十年前的原始底稿已經被大火燒光了。但他不知道，作為一名法醫，我永遠會為死者保留一份微縮膠卷底片。」\n\n裴以安接過公文包，指尖觸碰到冰冷堅硬的鈦合金密碼盒。\n\n「這裡面，是林清源遇害當晚枕骨粉碎性骨折的全部顯微攝影底片，以及楚天成當年向十三位專家行賄的原始匯款存根。」顧志明深深注視著裴以安，眼底泛起一層釋然的淚光，「今晚大劇院的次聲波，只是一場引蛇出洞的戲碼。我真正的目的，是逼楚天成在全市面前認罪，並將這份跨越三十年的證詞，交到全濱江唯一不會妥協的法醫手裡。」\n\n老周深吸了一口氣，默默收起手槍，上前一把抓住了顧志明的胳膊：「老顧……把東西交出來，跟我們下樓。市檢察院和紀委的人已經在樓下等著了，三十年前的帳，我們一起去法庭上算乾淨！」\n\n「法庭？」顧志明搖了搖頭，嘴角泛起一抹決絕的微笑，「我是一個雙手沾滿謊言的法醫，我沒有資格以證人的身分走出這座大樓。」\n\n突然，顧志明的身軀猛烈抽搐了一下！\n\n他的呼吸驟然停止，整個人如同一座被抽去支柱的坍塌積木，直挺挺地向後方的天台懸崖仰面倒去！\n\n「老顧！！」老周撕心裂肺地大吼一聲，猛撲上去死死抓住了顧志明的風衣領口！\n\n「不是自殺，是多發性骨髓瘤誘發的惡性高鈣血症心律失常！」裴以安厲聲喝道，一個箭步跨上前，雙膝跪在冰冷泥濘的積水中，一把扯開顧志明的襯衫！\n\n胸外按壓、氣道開放、頸動脈博動監測！\n\n裴以安的雙手疊加在一起，精準按壓在顧志明胸骨中下三分之一處，骨骼在重壓下發出令人牙酸的摩擦聲，但他手上的動作沒有一絲停滯與遲疑！\n\n「裴……以安……放手……」顧志明渙散的瞳孔在閃電下劇烈顫動，乾裂的嘴唇微弱地翕動著，「讓我……死在林清源死去的……雨夜裡……」\n\n「閉嘴！」\n\n裴以安一邊進行著精準的胸外心臟復甦，一邊冷厲地注視著老人垂死的雙眼，聲音像淬火的精鋼般砸進雨幕：\n\n「法醫的職責是讓死者說話，而不是替罪人安排殉道的舞台！」\n\n「三十年前你用謊言埋葬了真相，三十年後，你休想用死亡逃避法律的審判！」\n\n「活下去，顧志明！你必須親口站在證人席上，向三十年前的林清源說出那句遲到的道歉！」\n\n「噗——！」\n\n一口憋在氣管深處的淤血從顧志明口中狂噴而出！\n\n伴隨著一聲劇烈的心臟搏動，老人的胸膛猛地劇烈起伏，大口大口地重新吸入了冰冷清冽的夜雨空氣！\n\n老周整個人脫力般坐在泥水裡，仰頭任由暴雨沖刷著通紅的眼眶，隨後狠狠抹了一把臉，對著對講機嘶吼道：\n\n「呼叫指揮中心！這裡是周成林！檔案大樓天台發現關鍵證人顧志明，立即派遣救護車與擔架組！三十年前的案子……我們破了！！」\n\n雨幕漸漸平息，東方天際的地平線上，一抹微弱的魚肚白正穿透重重烏雲，悄然破曉。\n\n【全書終局倒數 · 第十六章完】","rawContentEn":"# Chapter 16: The Rain-Night Denouement on the Archives Rooftop\n\nGales sweeping off the river lashed freezing rain like razor blades against the iron portal atop the twelfth floor of the Public Security Bureau's aged Archives Building.\n\n9:15 in the evening.\n\nErected in 1982, the gray-brick repository had long been marked for demolition; its elevators had ceased operating half a decade ago, leaving the stairwells heavy with the sour stench of damp paper mold and pulverized concrete dust.\n\nHoisting his tactical searchlight, Old Zhou wheezed as he shoved open the final rusted iron door leading out to the rooftop, his combat boots splashing frantic sprays across the yellowed concrete puddles.\n\n\"Little Pei... slow down! My old knees... climbed a hundred and eighty steps today, my menisci are ground to dust!\" Old Zhou swiped rain from his brow, his other hand fiercely guarding his heroic pink thermos inside his fleece pocket. \"Are you certain the coordinates embedded in Chen Weiguo's ribs pointed straight to the lightning rod plinth on this damned archives tower?\"\n\n\"The microchip utilizes early-generation military VHF transponder technology, with an operational detection radius under fifty meters,\" Pei Yi'an stepped across the threshold, his trench coat snapping violently in the gale. On the screen of his handheld RF spectrum analyzer, a crimson dot pulsed twice per second, locking into absolute convergence with the telecommunications tower ahead.\n\nA whip of lightning tore through leaden clouds, drenching the rooftop in blinding white brilliance.\n\nBeneath the angled steel telecommunications mast perched on the roof's edge, a tall, slender silhouette stood with his back turned, motionless amidst the torrential rain.\n\nDraped in an oversized black storm mac whose hem whipped wildly in the gusts, the figure had a slight hunch, his left shoulder visibly higher than the right, leaning upon a custom orthopedic cane crafted of carbon fiber and pure titanium.\n\nBeside his feet rested a vintage cowhide briefcase from the 1980s, its scuffed leather face still bearing the faded gold-stamped imprint: **[Binjiang Municipal Public Security Bureau · Criminalistics Division · Forensic Examiner Sole Issue]**.\n\n\"Thirty years, Old Zhou, and that wheezing of yours on the stairs hasn't changed a bit.\"\n\nA gravelly, aged, yet profoundly familiar and gentle voice drifted through the screeching storm, reaching Old Zhou's ears.\n\nOld Zhou's entire frame froze rigid on the spot, his flashlight nearly slipping from his grasp.\n\n\"That voice...\" Old Zhou's pupils dilated in pure disbelief, his pitch rising in shock. \"Old Gu?! Gu Zhiming?! How could it possibly be you?!\"\n\nThe figure leaning on the titanium crutch turned slowly around.\n\nA jagged flash illuminated his features—a gaunt face etched with deep, painful furrows, temples dusted with frost-white hair, bearing a pair of rimless gold spectacles strikingly similar to Pei Yi'an's own.\n\nGu Zhiming—former Chief of the Bureau's Forensic Pathology Division, Old Zhou's field partner when he joined the force thirty years ago, and Pei Yi'an's sponsoring mentor when he entered the Ministry of Justice's Forensic Research Institute seven years back!\n\nThree years prior, he had retired on medical grounds due to advanced myelodysplastic syndrome, vanishing completely from the public eye.\n\n\"Teacher Gu,\" Pei Yi'an stopped, his countenance cool as frost, though his knuckles tightened almost imperceptibly at his side. \"From the dual-axis hairspring micro-regulation slide on that bone bow at the Grand Theatre, to Chen Weiguo's articulated skeleton inside the thirteenth freezer... all the specimen preservation protocols and micro-metric dissection techniques originated from your doctoral patents thirty years ago.\"\n\n\"Little Pei, you are the finest student I ever mentored—surpassing both myself and Lin Qingyuan in our prime,\" Gu Zhiming took off his rain-flecked glasses, wiping them with a dry chamois cloth. \"The dead do not lie; the bones record all. Those were the very first words I imparted to you when I brought you into the morgue.\"\n\n\"Then why did you become 'The Ferryman'?!\" Old Zhou roared with bloodshot eyes, stepping forward with his gun trembling toward his former comrade. \"When Dr. Lin died thirty years ago, your signature was on the autopsy report! You were the one who certified it as an 'accidental drowning'! You took Chu Tiancheng's blood money and climbed the bureaucratic ladder, and thirty years later you have the gall to orchestrate vigilante executions with human bones?!\"\n\n\"Old Zhou, you truly believe I did it for promotions and gold?\" Gu Zhiming's lips twisted into a tragic, self-mocking smile as he unbuttoned his trench coat.\n\nBeneath his navy shirt sat an intricate orthopedic exoskeleton cage of medical-grade titanium, rigidly encasing his entire thoracic and lumbar spine.\n\n\"Look here, Little Pei. Perform an ante-mortem biopsy on your old teacher,\" Gu Zhiming pointed to his deformed spinal curvature, speaking as calmly as if presenting an anatomical specimen.\n\nPei Yi'an stepped forward, his eyes fixing on the spinal fixture spanning from T7 down to L2.\n\n\"Diffuse osteolytic lesions across the thoracolumbar vertebrae, punched-out cortical defects, accompanied by severe pathological compression fractures,\" Pei Yi'an stated the clinical verdict without flinching. \"End-stage multiple myeloma with bone metastases invading spinal nerve roots. You have at most three months to live.\"\n\n\"Indeed, three months,\" Gu Zhiming replaced his spectacles, rain streaming down the glass. \"Thirty years ago, Chu Tiancheng strode into my morgue flanked by ministerial directives, slamming a solid brass surgical mallet beside Lin Qingyuan's corpse. He told me that if I refused to sign that drowning certificate, my newborn daughter in her hospital incubator would 'suffocate in an unfortunate medical accident.'\"\n\nOld Zhou's gun hand convulsed, the weathered contours of his face twisting in visceral anguish.\n\n\"I capitulated. I signed my name. I played the coward and accomplice for thirty years!\" Gu Zhiming's withered fingers clamped around his cane until his veins bulged. \"Lin Qingyuan was my dearest friend; Chen Weiguo died attempting to secure evidence for him. For thirty years, every patent Chu Tiancheng usurped metastasized into cancer within my marrow! Every bone in my body aches every second—it is Lin and Chen crying out from the grave!\"\n\n\"So you tracked down the exiled Qin Mo, took him as your disciple, and plotted this thirty-year retribution?\" Pei Yi'an asked.\n\n\"Qin Mo was the scalpel; I was the one drafting the anatomical roadmap,\" Gu Zhiming bent down, lifting the vintage leather case and holding it toward Pei Yi'an. \"Chu Tiancheng believed the original 1994 manuscripts perished in the fire. He never knew that a forensic pathologist will always preserve an encrypted microfilm negative for the departed.\"\n\nPei Yi'an accepted the briefcase, his fingertips meeting the cold, unyielding titanium security container within.\n\n\"Inside lie the complete polarizing micro-photographs of Lin Qingyuan's comminuted occipital fracture taken that fateful night, along with the original remittance vouchers Chu Tiancheng paid out to bribe thirteen corrupt experts,\" Gu Zhiming looked deep into Pei Yi'an's eyes, a solitary tear of release welling in his aged gaze. \"Tonight's infrasound demonstration at the Grand Theatre was merely a gambit to draw the serpent from its hole. My ultimate goal was to force Chu Tiancheng's public ruin and hand this thirty-year deposition into the hands of the only forensic pathologist in Binjiang who never compromises.\"\n\nTaking a deep breath, Old Zhou holstered his sidearm and stepped forward to grasp Gu Zhiming's sleeve: \"Old Gu... now that you've passed the torch, come down with us. The Procuratorate and the anti-corruption task force are waiting below. The debts of thirty years ago—we will settle them together in a court of law!\"\n\n\"A court of law?\" Gu Zhiming shook his head, a resolute smile gracing his pale lips. \"I am a medical examiner whose hands were drenched in lies. I hold no moral right to walk out of this structure as a witness.\"\n\nSuddenly, Gu Zhiming's body jerked in violent spasm!\n\nHis respiration halted abruptly, his frame collapsing like a scaffold stripped of its supports, tipping backward toward the unguarded ledge!\n\n\"Old Gu!!\" Old Zhou yelled at the top of his lungs, hurling himself forward to seize the lapels of the elder's coat!\n\n\"It is no suicide—it is malignant hypercalcemic arrhythmia triggered by multiple myeloma!\" Pei Yi'an barked, dropping to his knees in the freezing rainwater and ripping open Gu Zhiming's shirt!\n\nChest compressions, airway clearance, carotid pulse check!\n\nLocking his palms together, Pei Yi'an delivered rapid, rhythmic thrusts over the lower third of Gu Zhiming's sternum. Brittle bones creaked under the immense pressure, yet his technique showed neither hesitation nor retreat!\n\n\"Pei... Yi'an... let me go...\" Gu Zhiming's dilating pupils flickered under the lightning, his dry lips parting feebly. \"Let me... die in the same rain... where Lin Qingyuan perished...\"\n\n\"Shut up!\"\n\nContinuing uninterrupted compressions, Pei Yi'an stared into the dying man's eyes, his words striking like tempered steel through the squall:\n\n\"A forensic pathologist's duty is to give voice to the deceased, not to stage martyrdom for sinners!\"\n\n\"Thirty years ago you buried the truth beneath a lie; thirty years later, do not dream of escaping justice through the convenience of death!\"\n\n\"Survive, Gu Zhiming! You must stand in that witness box with your own breath and deliver that thirty-year-overdue apology to Lin Qingyuan!\"\n\n*Cough—!*\n\nA clot of stagnant blood trapped within the trachea erupted from Gu Zhiming's mouth!\n\nSpurred by a resurgent pulse, the old pathologist's chest heaved violently, dragging in ragged, greedy draughts of freezing night air!\n\nSlumping limp into the muddy wash, Old Zhou tilted his head back, letting the rain scour his bloodshot eyes before wiping his face and bellowing into his radio:\n\n\"Dispatch, this is Zhou Chenglin! Critical witness Gu Zhiming secured atop the Archives Building—request immediate paramedic and stretcher units! That thirty-year case... we just cracked it wide open!!\"\n\nThe rain began to taper. Along the eastern horizon, a faint sliver of pale dawn pierced through the broken clouds, heralding the sunrise.\n\n[Grand Finale Countdown · End of Chapter 16]"},{"id":17,"rawContent":"# 第十七章：三十年前的病理底稿\n\n清晨五點三十分，漫天暴雨終於漸漸止歇。\n\n微弱的青灰色晨光穿透市局物證鑒定中心的百葉窗，將冰冷的解剖台與滿室的儀器映照出一層朦朧的金屬微光。\n\n經過一整夜的連續奮戰，老周臉上的皺紋深得像被刻刀雕鑿過，眼球布滿猩紅的血絲。他坐在物證顯微鏡旁的轉椅上，雙手捧著那隻褪色的粉紅色保溫杯，熱騰騰的白霧在鏡片前嫋嫋升起。\n\n「小李已經從麻醉狀態裡醒過來了，那小子年輕體格好，除了脖子落枕沒受別的傷。」老周喝了一口參茶，聲音沙啞得如同砂紙摩擦，「老顧在警犬基地直屬醫院的特護病房裡，紀委和市檢察院專案組的四名同志二十四小時就地監護，血壓總算穩住了。」\n\n「多發性骨髓瘤引發的高鈣血症危象暫時得到了抑制，但他的心肌與腎功能已經出現不可逆衰竭。」裴以安換上了一件一塵不染的白色實驗服，神情依舊冷靜專注，「顧志明的生命只剩下最後幾十天。這隻箱子裡的底稿，是他用三十年痛苦折磨換來的最後證言。」\n\n物證檢驗台中央，赫然擺放著從天台帶回的那隻八十年代牛皮公文包。\n\n公文包內側，那座純鈦打造的八位機械密碼盒已被蘇棠用工業內窺鏡與聲學共振儀成功破解。\n\n隨著一聲沉悶的「喀嗒」脆響，厚達兩公分的鈦合金蓋板緩緩彈開。\n\n沒有發霉的腐味，也沒有任何灰塵。\n\n密碼盒內壁被高純度的聚四氟乙烯膜密封，內部充填著乾燥惰性氬氣。五個被獨立封裝在真空防酸聚酯套管中的深棕色檔案袋，靜靜整齊地排列在天鵝絨凹槽內。\n\n裴以安戴上無粉丁腈手套，用扁平竹鑷小心翼翼地夾出最上方那份泛黃的手寫原稿。\n\n那是三十年前市立醫院病理研究所特製的網格報告紙，抬頭用深藍色油墨印著早已停用的院徽。而在報告首頁右下角，赫然簽署著一個蒼勁有力的名字：**林清源**。\n\n簽署日期：**一九九四年七月十七日，凌晨一點四十分**——正是林清源在二號乾塢墜江前六個小時！\n\n「三十年前楚天成對外宣稱，病理所的那場大火把林博士所有的原始實驗記錄全部付之一炬。」老周湊上前，眼神熾熱，「老顧居然把這份原本藏得這麼深！」\n\n「這不是普通的研究日誌，這是林清源生前完成的最後一份《重組抗腫瘤多肽生物製劑（代號9407）三期臨床安全性評估報告》。」裴以安將手稿平鋪在超高解析度多光譜掃描儀的冷光源載物台上。\n\n掃描儀發出輕微的嗡鳴，藍紫色的線性光束自上而下緩緩掃過紙頁。\n\n電腦螢幕上，三十年前手寫的墨跡與化學分子結構式被瞬間放大數百倍，清晰地呈現在三人眼前。\n\n「看第三十八頁的細胞毒理學圖表。」裴以安修長的手指落在觸控屏上，「林清源在這份報告中明確指出，楚天成主導研發的這款所謂『抗癌神藥』，在動物實驗與早期試用者身上展現出了致命的遠期骨髓毒性。」\n\n「骨髓毒性？！」老周心頭猛地一震。\n\n「它會誘發造血幹細胞基因突變，在用藥後五至十年內，導致不可逆的惡性骨髓異常增生以及瀰漫性溶骨性病變。」裴以安的聲音沉冷如鐵，「這根本不是治病救人的神藥，而是一種披著抗癌外衣的慢性劇毒基因破壞劑。」\n\n「我的天……」後座上的蘇棠捂住了嘴巴，臉色煞白，「楚氏製藥三十年前就是靠著這款藥的專利完成上市融資的！當年全市有數千名癌症患者服用了這款改頭換面的昂貴製劑！」\n\n「林清源當年堅持要向國家衛生部提交緊急叫停報告，並要求封存銷毀全部生產線。」裴以安翻開第二個檔案袋，取出了一卷三十五毫米的顯微攝影黑白底片，「這觸動了楚天成背後那張由資本與權力織成的龐大黑網。」\n\n裴以安將底片插入透射顯微掃描槽。\n\n螢幕上頓時顯現出一張張令人觸目驚心的顯微照片——那是一具顱骨的枕骨大孔邊緣，高倍放大下的骨質粉碎截面。\n\n「看骨折邊緣的凹陷弧度。」裴以安調整偏振光對比度，「三十年前顧志明頂著死亡威脅，在偽造『溺亡』報告的同時，偷偷用微距相機拍攝下了林清源枕骨的真實創口。」\n\n「這是一處直徑約兩點五公分的半圓形凹陷性骨折，創口底部伴有金屬鈍器反覆擊打形成的『疊瓦狀骨裂紋』。」裴以安的手指在螢幕上精準勾勒出骨折輪廓，「這種特定的金屬撞擊截面，只有外科醫生最常用的八角形純銅敲骨錘才能形成。」\n\n「楚天成！」老周咬牙切齒地吐出這個名字。\n\n「不只是楚天成。」裴以安冷冷地移動游標，放大枕骨顳側一處極其隱蔽的次級微裂隙。\n\n「你看這裡。」裴以安眼神驟變，「在枕骨大孔左側兩公分處，還存在第二處平行的線性骨折！這處骨折的表面殘留著一道極其特殊的凹槽印記——寬四毫米，長七毫米，邊緣帶有微型鋸齒狀的徽章花紋。」\n\n「徽章花紋？！」老周愣住了，「這是什麼東西留下的？」\n\n「這是重力揮拳擊打面部或後腦時，金屬指環或印章戒指直接撞擊骨質造成的特徵性壓痕。」裴以安調取市局法醫創傷資料庫進行三維拓撲比對，「當年二號乾塢的謀殺現場，除了手持手術錘的楚天成，現場還有第二個人！」\n\n「而且那個人的拳力足以擊裂成年男性的顱骨，手上戴著一枚刻有特定家族或機構紋章的純金印章戒指！」\n\n老周的瞳孔劇烈收縮，腦海中一道塵封了三十年的恐怖記憶如狂瀾般翻江倒海！\n\n「印章戒指……」老周的嘴唇開始發白，額頭青筋暴跳，「三十年前兼任市立醫院名譽院長、主管全市醫藥審批的那位前任副市長宋懷德……他的左手食指上，常年戴著一枚象徵省醫學會終身理事的重金家族印章！」\n\n「正是他。」裴以安拉開第三個檔案袋，裡面赫然滑出了一疊泛黃泛脆的銀行跨行劃撥原始憑證！\n\n在那些一九九四年七月十八日開具的加急匯款單上，收款人那一欄，赫然用鋼筆工整地填寫著宋懷德親屬名下的海外信託帳戶！\n\n受賄金額：**三百二十萬美元！**\n\n在三十年前，這是一筆足以買下半座濱江港口的天文數字！\n\n「林清源的死不是一場單純的商業謀殺，而是一場由官員、資本家與腐敗專家聯手策劃的滅口行動。」裴以安將所有證據檔案整齊碼放在防護盒內，目光冷冽如霜，「楚天成負責出資與動手，宋懷德負責壓下行政調查，而顧志明則被逼簽下偽證。」\n\n就在此時，老周腰間的加密警用手機突然發出了一陣尖銳刺耳的警報鈴聲！\n\n老周猛地抓起手機按下了免提鍵。\n\n電話那頭，市局刑偵支隊副隊長急促得幾乎變調的喊聲在大廳內炸響：\n\n「周隊！市中心醫院ICU病房出事了！」\n\n「楚天成剛才在監護室內突發急性呼吸衰竭，瞳孔擴散！醫生在他的靜脈滴注液中檢測出了未標識的高濃度氯化鉀雜質！」\n\n「有人要搶在檢察院提審前……在醫院把楚天成徹底滅口！」\n\n老周一把抓起桌上的警槍與那隻粉紅色保溫杯，眼中寒芒暴漲：\n\n「宋懷德動手了！他要切斷最後的活口鏈條！」\n\n裴以安扣上手提箱的鎖扣，銀色箱體在晨光中反射出冷冽的銀輝：\n\n「周隊，帶上除顫儀和解毒劑。死人已經說完了他們的證詞，現在，輪到我們去保住活人的呼吸了！」","rawContentEn":"# Chapter 17: The Pathology Manuscript from Thirty Years Ago\n\nAt 5:30 in the morning, the torrential deluge finally began to subside.\n\nPale, slate-gray dawn filtered through the blinds of the Forensic Identification Center, casting a hazy metallic luster across the stainless dissection tables and high-precision instruments.\n\nFollowing a night of relentless exertion, the lines on Old Zhou's face looked as though gouged with an engraver's chisel, his conjunctiva veined with crimson spiderwebs. Perched upon a swivel stool beside the polarizing microscope, he cradled his faded pink thermos with both hands as curls of steam drifted lazily before his eyes.\n\n\"Young Li has regained consciousness from the sedation; the kid's got youth on his side, suffering nothing worse than a stiff neck,\" Old Zhou rasped, taking a sip of ginseng brew, his voice scratching like coarse sandpaper. \"Old Gu is settled in the intensive care pavilion of the Police Hospital. Four investigators from the Discipline Commission and the Procuratorate are maintaining twenty-four-hour bedside vigil; his hemodynamics have finally stabilized.\"\n\n\"The hypercalcemic crisis precipitated by multiple myeloma has been temporarily quelled, yet his myocardial and renal reserves have suffered irreversible decline,\" Pei Yi'an remarked, pulling on a pristine white laboratory coat, his focus sharp and unwavering. \"Gu Zhiming has merely weeks remaining. The manuscripts inside this case represent the final deposition he purchased with thirty years of private agony.\"\n\nIn the center of the forensic workbench sat the 1980s cowhide briefcase retrieved from the rooftop.\n\nInside, the eight-digit mechanical security container of solid titanium had already been breached by Su Tang utilizing an industrial borescope and acoustic resonance probes.\n\nWith a dull, heavy click, the two-centimeter-thick titanium alloy lid sprang gently ajar.\n\nThere was neither musty odor nor a single grain of dust.\n\nThe interior casing was hermetically lined with virgin PTFE film and purged with dry argon gas. Five dark brown dossier pouches, individually sealed within vacuum-evacuated acid-free Mylar sleeves, lay aligned in velvet cradles.\n\nDonning powder-free nitrile gloves, Pei Yi'an wielded flat bamboo forceps to lift the top manuscript of yellowed parchment with exquisite care.\n\nIt was printed on the gridded examination leaves exclusive to the Municipal Hospital Pathology Institute thirty years ago, its header bearing the decommissioned emblem in indigo ink. And in the lower right margin of the title folio stood an assertive, elegant signature: **Lin Qingyuan**.\n\nDate of signature: **July 17, 1994, at 1:40 AM**—precisely six hours prior to Lin Qingyuan's fatal plunge at Dry Dock No. 2!\n\n\"Thirty years ago, Chu Tiancheng told the world that the laboratory fire had incinerated every scrap of Dr. Lin's research,\" Old Zhou leaned forward, his eyes blazing. \"To think Old Gu stashed the original manuscript away so deep!\"\n\n\"This is no ordinary laboratory notebook; this is the final completed draft of Lin Qingyuan's 'Phase III Clinical Safety Assessment of Recombinant Anti-Neoplastic Polypeptide Biologic (Project 9407),'\" Pei Yi'an laid the manuscript across the cold-light stage of the ultra-high-resolution multispectral scanner.\n\nThe scanner hummed quietly, a violet laser line passing smoothly down the aged page.\n\nOn the primary workstation monitor, three-decade-old carbon ink notations and complex molecular structural diagrams were magnified hundreds of times in razor-sharp clarity.\n\n\"Observe the cellular toxicology schematics on page thirty-eight,\" Pei Yi'an's finger traced the high-resolution display. \"Lin Qingyuan explicitly demonstrated here that this purported 'miracle oncological remedy' spearheaded by Chu Tiancheng exhibited catastrophic long-term myelotoxicity in animal models and early compassionate-use cohorts.\"\n\n\"Myelotoxicity?!\" Old Zhou's chest seized.\n\n\"It triggers mutagenic cascades within hematopoietic stem cells, culminating five to ten years post-administration in refractory myelodysplasia and diffuse osteolytic devastation,\" Pei Yi'an said, his voice hard as iron. \"It was never a therapeutic salvation; it was a slow-acting mutagenic poison dressed in clinical laurels.\"\n\n\"Good heavens...\" In the rear seat, Su Tang covered her mouth, all color draining from her cheeks. \"Chu Bio-Pharmaceutical went public thirty years ago based entirely on the patents for that formulation! Thousands of cancer patients across the province were dosed with that rebranded, exorbitant compound!\"\n\n\"Lin Qingyuan insisted on submitting an emergency injunction to the Ministry of Health, demanding the immediate impoundment and destruction of all manufacturing lines,\" Pei Yi'an opened the second sleeve, extracting a roll of 35-millimeter black-and-white photomicrographic film. \"That conviction directly threatened the corrupt syndicate of capital and political influence standing behind Chu Tiancheng.\"\n\nPei Yi'an fed the strip into the transmission micro-scanner.\n\nHigh-contrast macro-images materialized upon the displays—polarized cross-sections of the comminuted fractures encircling the foramen magnum of an adult cranium.\n\n\"Observe the concave curvature along the fracture margins,\" Pei Yi'an dialed the polarizing contrast. \"Thirty years ago, even while under threat of immediate assassination, Gu Zhiming secretly captured macro-photographs of Lin Qingyuan's true occipital wound before signing the forged drowning certificate.\"\n\n\"This is a semicircular depressed fracture roughly 2.5 centimeters across, the base riddled with imbricated micro-fissures indicative of repetitive blunt impact,\" Pei Yi'an traced the perimeter on-screen. \"Such a distinct geometry can only be produced by an octagonal solid-brass bone mallet standard to orthopedic surgery.\"\n\n\"Chu Tiancheng!\" Old Zhou spat the name through clenched teeth.\n\n\"Not Chu Tiancheng alone,\" Pei Yi'an moved the cursor, zooming into a secondary, faint micro-fracture along the temporo-occipital boundary.\n\n\"Look here,\" Pei Yi'an's gaze sharpened. \"Two centimeters lateral to the foramen magnum lies a second linear fissure! Imprinted upon the cortical bone is an anomalous indentation—four millimeters wide, seven millimeters long, its borders serrated with the crest of a crest-like insignia.\"\n\n\"A crest pattern?!\" Old Zhou blinked. \"What on earth left that mark?\"\n\n\"It is the pathognomonic imprint left when a heavy blow is delivered with a fist bearing a signet ring,\" Pei Yi'an ran a 3D topological query against the Bureau's trauma biomechanics library. \"At Dry Dock No. 2 that night, alongside Chu Tiancheng with his surgical mallet, stood a second perpetrator!\"\n\n\"A man whose striking force fractured an adult calvarium, wearing a solid gold signet ring engraved with a specific familial or institutional seal!\"\n\nOld Zhou's pupils constricted into tiny dots, thirty-year-old memories surging like an ocean tempest!\n\n\"A signet ring...\" Old Zhou's lips paled, veins bulging on his forehead. \"Thirty years ago, the former Deputy Mayor who concurrently served as Honorary President of Municipal Hospital and regulated all regional pharmaceutical approvals—Song Huaide... He wore a heavy gold family signet ring on his left index finger, marking his lifetime directorship in the Provincial Medical Association!\"\n\n\"Precisely him,\" Pei Yi'an slid open the third dossier sleeve, spilling forth a stack of brittle, yellowed interbank transfer slips!\n\nUpon those expedited wire drafts dated July 18, 1994, the beneficiary line was inscribed in meticulous fountain-pen script: an overseas trust account registered under Song Huaide's immediate kin!\n\nThe sum: **$3.2 million USD!**\n\nThirty years ago, that was an astronomical fortune capable of purchasing half the deepwater terminals of Binjiang Port!\n\n\"Lin Qingyuan's demise was never a mere commercial assassination; it was a state-level silencing conspiracy orchestrated by a corrupt official, an unscrupulous venture capitalist, and complicit scientists,\" Pei Yi'an filed the folios into the containment case, his stare as unbending as frost. \"Chu Tiancheng provided the muscle and capital, Song Huaide quashed the judicial inquiry, and Gu Zhiming was coerced into signing perjury.\"\n\nAt that exact second, the encrypted tactical transceiver on Old Zhou's duty belt shrieked with an ear-splitting alarm!\n\nOld Zhou snatched the handset and slapped the speakerphone button.\n\nFrom the receiver, the frantic, cracked voice of the Detachment Deputy Commander erupted through the lab:\n\n\"Captain Zhou! Disaster at Central Hospital ICU!\"\n\n\"Chu Tiancheng went into acute respiratory arrest five minutes ago with blown pupils! Attending physicians found trace signatures of lethal potassium chloride spiked into his saline line!\"\n\n\"Someone is attempting to liquidate Chu Tiancheng in the hospital... before the Procuratorate can depose him!\"\n\nGrabbing his service pistol and his pink thermos from the table, Old Zhou's eyes flared with cold fire:\n\n\"Song Huaide is making his move! He's severing the final living link!\"\n\nPei Yi'an snapped the latches of his field kit shut, the silver case reflecting the cold morning sun:\n\n\"Captain Zhou, take the defibrillator and the potassium antagonists. The dead have concluded their testimonies; now it is our duty to preserve the respiration of the living!\""},{"id":18,"rawContent":"# 第十八章：誰是真正的擺渡人\n\n清晨六點十五分，刺耳的警笛聲撕裂了濱江市中心醫院上空的薄霧。\n\n老桑塔納警車一個甩尾猛停在急診大樓門前，老周與裴以安推開車門，快步衝進專用醫梯，直撲十六樓的心內科重症監護室（ICU）。\n\n監護室的雙扇彈簧門被撞開的瞬間，刺目的紅色搶救指示燈正瘋狂閃爍，心電監護儀發出一陣尖銳無比的長鳴：\n\n「滴————————」\n\n螢幕上的波形已經徹底拉成了一條死寂的直線！\n\n「室顫轉心搏驟停！除顫無效！胸外按壓無效！」主治醫師滿頭冷汗，手持除顫電極板聲嘶力竭地大喊，「靜脈血鉀濃度高達八點五毫摩爾每升，心肌電生理已經完全崩潰了！」\n\n病床上，原本不可一世的百億富豪楚天成此時雙眼翻白，面色紫紺，四肢僵直如鐵，那條正滴著生理鹽水的輸液管濾網處，殘留著微量泛著淡黃色的不明結晶。\n\n「滾開，讓我來。」\n\n一道冰冷而沉靜的聲音直接打斷了慌亂的搶救團隊。\n\n裴以安大步上前，甚至連實驗服都沒脫，右手一揮便精準扯下了那條被投毒的輸液管。他的指尖以令人窒息的速度掃過搶救車上的藥品架：\n\n「百分之十葡萄糖酸鈣二十毫升，立刻靜脈緩注，五微秒內對抗鉀離子心肌毒性！」\n\n「高糖五十毫升加正規胰島素十單位，建立第二靜脈通路，促使細胞外鉀離子迅速內轉！」\n\n「百分之五碳酸氫鈉一百毫升快速靜脈滴注，糾正代謝性酸中毒！」\n\n兩名護士被裴以安那股不容置疑的上位醫學威壓所震懾，幾乎是本能地按照他的指令飛快推注藥物。\n\n裴以安一把抓過除顫儀的手柄，將能量檔位旋鈕重重擰至「360焦耳」的最大極限！\n\n「導電膏塗抹完畢！」\n\n「所有人離開病床！」裴以安眼神凌厲如刀，雙臂肌肉緊繃，將兩具沉重的電極板狠狠砸在楚天成的右鎖骨下與左乳頭外側胸壁上！\n\n「充電完畢——放電！」\n\n「砰！」\n\n楚天成的上半身在強大的電流衝擊下猛然彈起數十公分，隨後重重砸回病床上！\n\n一秒、兩秒、三秒。\n\n心電監護儀在死寂中沉寂了整整四次微弱的電流雜波。\n\n緊接著——\n\n「滴……滴……滴……」\n\n那條平直的死亡直線，突然頑強地跳出了一道高聳陡峭的QRS波群！\n\n竇性心律，每分鐘五十八次！\n\n主治醫師脫力般扶著搶救車，整個人癱坐在椅子上，看向裴以安的眼神如同看著一個從閻王殿搶人的怪物。\n\n病床上的楚天成猛地抽搐了一下，喉嚨裡發出一陣風箱般的乾嘔，渾濁恐懼的眼睛終於緩緩睜開。\n\n映入他眼簾的，不是死神的鐮刀，而是裴以安那張在無影燈下冷峻如冰霜的面孔，以及身旁老周手中黑洞洞的九二式手槍。\n\n「楚天成，」老周上前一步，粗糙的大手一把攥住楚天成的病號服衣領，將他整個人生生提了起來，「氯化鉀致死量注射。給你看守監護室的保鏢收了五百萬封口費，剛才在安全通道被我們當場按死。你為那條老狗賣了三十年的命，人家轉頭就把你當成一條病死狗扔進垃圾桶！」\n\n楚天成渾身劇烈顫抖，眼淚、鼻涕與冷汗混雜著湧出臉頰，三十年商海沉浮積攢的尊嚴在這一刻被徹底碾碎成齏粉。\n\n「宋……宋懷德……」楚天成聲音嘶啞得如同含著碎玻璃，「那個畜生……他要殺我……他要殺我滅口……」\n\n「宋懷德現在在哪裡？！」老周怒吼，額頭青筋暴凸。\n\n「濱江國際機場……西區公務機停機坪……」楚天成癱在枕頭上，斷斷續續地吐出真相，「今早八點……他包下了飛往瑞士的灣流私人商務機……他把當年所有參與審批的官員名冊與分紅帳本全帶在隨身保險箱裡……只要他飛出國境……我就成了唯一的替死鬼……」\n\n老周猛地抬腕看錶——清晨六點三十分！\n\n距離宋懷德的私人飛機起飛，僅剩最後九十分鐘！\n\n「立刻通知交警支隊，對通往機場的高速路段實施全線交通管制！特警支隊全體登車，封鎖停機坪！」老周對著對講機厲聲下達指令。\n\n然而，站在一旁的裴以安卻突然皺起了眉頭。\n\n他的目光落在大廳長椅上那台始終開著的加密戰術終端上。\n\n自從半小時前離開市局物證中心開始，那台負責為他們監控全城天網與微波頻譜的電腦，便再也沒有發送過任何一條語音回報。\n\n「周隊，蘇棠呢？」裴以安的聲音驟然降到了冰點。\n\n「小蘇？」老周愣了一下，下意識摸出手機，「剛才出發前，那丫頭說要留在局裡物證室替我們做微縮膠卷的數字化修復……」\n\n老周撥通了蘇棠的號碼。\n\n聽筒裡傳來的，卻是一陣冰冷機械的系統提示音：\n\n『對不起，您撥打的號碼已不在服務區。』\n\n裴以安一把奪過終端電腦，指尖在鍵盤上快如殘影般敲擊出一連串底層代碼。\n\n螢幕上瞬間跳出了一道市局人事檔案庫的最高權限解密彈窗！\n\n彈窗的正中央，赫然是一張三十年前市立醫院新生兒保溫箱的出生證明掃描件：\n\n**【新生兒姓名：林棠】**\n**【父親：林清源（市立醫院病理科主任）】**\n**【母親：蘇玉華（一九九四年七月因難產病逝）】**\n**【收養備註：一九九四年林清源遇害後，由蘇姓工兵家庭正式領養，更名為——蘇棠！】**\n\n老周的手機「啪嗒」一聲摔在地上，整個人如遭五雷轟頂，大腦一片空白：\n\n「小蘇……小蘇是林清源的女兒？！」\n\n「這就是『擺渡人』的完整拼圖。」裴以安合上筆記本，眼神深邃得彷彿能吞噬深淵，「顧志明提供三十年前的法醫證據與法律謀劃，秦墨負責打造精密絕倫的骨骼機關吸引警方注意，而真正坐鎮中樞、調配全城信號、引導我們一步步掀開黑幕的指揮大腦……正是林清源的女兒，蘇棠。」\n\n「她去機場了！」老周失聲大喊，「她知道宋懷德要跑！她根本沒打算讓宋懷德活著登機！」\n\n「她不會殺人。」裴以安提起勘查箱，大步衝向電梯，「如果是為了殺人，以她的黑客技術，早在半個月前就能黑進宋懷德的心臟起搏器。她要的是一場公開的處決，一場在全世界注視下的終極正義。」\n\n「但宋懷德身邊有八名持槍的境外私人保鏢！」老周一邊狂奔一邊咆哮，「那丫頭單槍匹馬衝過去，就是去送死！」\n\n雨後的朝陽刺破重重陰霾，將整座濱江機場高速公路染成一片赤金。\n\n黑色警車如離弦之箭般撕裂晨霧，向著最後的戰場狂飆而去。","rawContentEn":"# Chapter 18: Who is the True Ferryman\n\nAt 6:15 in the morning, piercing sirens shredded the pale mist hovering above Binjiang Central Hospital.\n\nThe aged Santana cruiser fishtailed to an emergency halt before the trauma center. Old Zhou and Pei Yi'an kicked their doors open, sprinting into the dedicated medical elevator to charge up to the sixteenth-floor Cardiac Intensive Care Unit (ICU).\n\nThe moment the double swinging doors of the unit burst open, the glaring crimson resuscitation beacons were flashing frantically, while the telemetry monitor wailed in an unrelenting, piercing screech:\n\n*BEEEEEEEEEEEEEP————*\n\nOn the screen, the waveform had flattened into an absolute, silent line of death!\n\n\"Ventricular fibrillation transitioned to full asystole! Shocks ineffective! Compressions failing!\" the attending physician shouted hoarsely, sweat dripping from his chin as he gripped the defibrillator paddles. \"Serum potassium spiked to 8.5 millimoles per liter—myocardial electrophysiology has collapsed completely!\"\n\nUpon the bed, the once-haughty billionaire Chu Tiancheng lay with eyes rolled back, skin cyanotic, limbs rigid as cast iron. In the drip chamber filter of his saline line clung faint, yellowish crystalline residues.\n\n\"Step aside. Let me through.\"\n\nAn icy, tranquil voice cut clean through the frantic medical team.\n\nPei Yi'an strode to the bedside, not even pausing to discard his lab coat, his right hand ripping away the poisoned IV line with practiced grace. His fingertips swept across the medication cart with breathtaking velocity:\n\n\"Ten percent calcium gluconate, twenty milliliters—slow IV push immediately to antagonize potassium cardiotoxicity at the cellular membrane!\"\n\n\"Fifty percent dextrose, fifty milliliters with ten units regular insulin—establish secondary peripheral line to drive extracellular potassium back into intracellular compartments!\"\n\n\"Five percent sodium bicarbonate, one hundred milliliters rapid infusion to correct metabolic acidosis!\"\n\nOverwhelmed by Pei Yi'an's supreme clinical authority, the two nurses responded instinctively, administering the emergency vials without a heartbeat of hesitation.\n\nSnatching the defibrillator handles, Pei Yi'an dialed the rotary selector firmly to its maximum output: \"360 Joules!\"\n\n\"Conductive gel applied!\"\n\n\"Clear the bed!\" Pei Yi'an's eyes were sharp as razors, his forearms corded with muscle as he slammed the heavy paddles down upon Chu Tiancheng's infraclavicular fossa and apical axillary line!\n\n\"Charged—shocking!\"\n\n*THUMP!*\n\nUnder the tremendous galvanic discharge, Chu Tiancheng's torso vaulted inches off the mattress before crashing back down upon the sheets!\n\nOne second. Two seconds. Three seconds.\n\nAcross the monitor, four cycles of electrical noise fluttered in dead silence.\n\nAnd then—\n\n*Beep... beep... beep...*\n\nOut of the flatline of oblivion leaped a towering, crisp QRS complex!\n\nSinus rhythm, fifty-eight beats per minute!\n\nThe attending physician slumped into a stool as all strength left his knees, staring at Pei Yi'an as if gazing upon a supernatural entity that had just wrestled a soul back from the underworld.\n\nUpon the gurney, Chu Tiancheng convulsed, dry heaves scraping through his throat like a rusted bellows before his terrified, clouded eyes fluttered open.\n\nWhat met his sight was no reaper's scythe, but Pei Yi'an's glacial features beneath the surgical lights, flanked by the dark muzzle of Old Zhou's service pistol.\n\n\"Chu Tiancheng,\" Old Zhou leaned in, his calloused fist twisting into the collar of the patient gown to hoist the tycoon upright. \"A lethal bolus of potassium chloride. The bodyguard stationed outside took five million in hush money; we pinned him down in the stairwell five minutes ago. You served that old mongrel for thirty years, and he disposed of you like roadkill the second the heat turned on!\"\n\nChu Tiancheng shook uncontrollably, tears, mucus, and cold sweat smearing his face, all the haughty dignity amassed across three decades of corporate dominion pulverized to dust.\n\n\"Song... Song Huaide...\" Chu Tiancheng rasped, his voice grinding like broken glass. \"That monster... he wanted me dead... wanted to silence me forever...\"\n\n\"Where is Song Huaide right now?!\" Old Zhou bellowed, veins standing out on his neck.\n\n\"Binjiang International Airport... West Apron Private Terminal...\" Chu Tiancheng collapsed back against the pillow, gasping the truth in ragged spurts. \"Eight o'clock this morning... he chartered a Gulfstream private jet to Switzerland... He took the original ledger listing every corrupt bureaucrat and kickback ledger in a security briefcase... The moment his jet leaves sovereign airspace... I am left as the sole scapegoat...\"\n\nOld Zhou snapped his wrist to check his watch—6:30 AM!\n\nBarely ninety minutes remained before Song Huaide's private flight took to the skies!\n\n\"Alert Traffic Command immediately—impose total tactical gridlock across all highway arteries heading toward the airport! Dispatch SWAT to encircle the private apron!\" Old Zhou barked into his shoulder mic.\n\nBeside him, however, Pei Yi'an's brow knitted into a sharp furrow.\n\nHis gaze arrested upon the ruggedized tactical laptop resting upon the corridor bench.\n\nEver since they departed the Bureau's Evidence Center half an hour ago, that terminal—tasked with monitoring municipal surveillance feeds and spectrum telemetry—had ceased relaying any voice updates.\n\n\"Captain Zhou, where is Su Tang?\" Pei Yi'an's voice dropped below zero.\n\n\"Little Su?\" Old Zhou paused, instinctively patting his pocket for his phone. \"Before we rolled out, the girl said she was staying behind in the digital lab to finish scanning the microfilms...\"\n\nOld Zhou speed-dialed Su Tang's private line.\n\nWhat answered through the earpiece was the flat, synthesized operator recording:\n\n*\"The subscriber you have dialed is currently unreachable or out of service area.\"*\n\nSnatching the laptop, Pei Yi'an's fingers blurred across the mechanical keyboard, punching out root-level decryption scripts.\n\nIn a flash, a top-secret clearance window from the Municipal Personnel Archives slammed onto the screen!\n\nCentered in the dossier was a digitized neonatal birth certificate from Municipal Hospital dated 1994:\n\n**[Infant Name: Lin Tang]**\n**[Father: Lin Qingyuan (Chief of Pathology, Municipal Hospital)]**\n**[Mother: Su Yuhua (Deceased July 1994 from post-partum complications)]**\n**[Adoption Registry: Following Lin Qingyuan's murder in 1994, legally adopted into the Su sapper family and renamed—Su Tang!]**\n\nOld Zhou's handset clattered onto the linoleum tiles, his mind turning completely blank as if struck by a lightning bolt:\n\n\"Little Su... Little Su is Lin Qingyuan's daughter?!\"\n\n\"This completes the puzzle of 'The Ferryman,'\" Pei Yi'an closed the laptop, his gaze as deep as a bottomless abyss. \"Gu Zhiming provided the historical forensic evidence and legal leverage; Qin Mo forged the mechanical osteological traps to command police mobilization; and the master conductor orchestrating citywide telemetry, leading us step by step to exhume the conspiracy from within the system... was Lin Qingyuan's daughter, Su Tang.\"\n\n\"She's at the airport!\" Old Zhou gasped in sudden panic. \"She knows Song Huaide is fleeing! She never intended to let him step foot onto that aircraft alive!\"\n\n\"She will not commit murder,\" Pei Yi'an said, hoisting his kit and striding into the elevator. \"If murder were her goal, her cyber skills could have hacked Song Huaide's pacemaker weeks ago. What she demands is a public adjudication—absolute, undeniable justice beneath the eyes of the entire world.\"\n\n\"But Song Huaide is guarded by eight armed private security contractors!\" Old Zhou roared as they sprinted. \"That girl charging in alone is marching straight into a meat grinder!\"\n\nMorning sun pierced through the dissipating squall, painting the asphalt ribbon of the Binjiang Airport Expressway in blazing gold.\n\nThe black cruiser surged forward like an arrow released from a bow, hurtling through the morning fog toward the final battlefield."},{"id":19,"rawContent":"# 第十九章：穿透迷霧的最後一柄手術刀\n\n清晨七點十五分，濱江國際機場西區公務機停機坪。\n\n晨霧如白色的輕紗在空曠平整的水泥跑道上緩緩流動，一架銀灰色的灣流G650公務機正發出低沉震耳的渦輪轟鳴，尾噴口噴吐出肉眼可見的熱浪，正在進行起飛前的最後地面檢查。\n\n舷梯下方，七十歲的前任副市長宋懷德身穿一件剪裁精良的深灰色羊絨大衣，左手夾著雪茄，右手緊緊攥著一隻鈦合金手提密碼箱。\n\n他的身側，八名身著深色西裝、戴著微型耳麥的境外安保人員正警惕地按著腋下的槍套，背靠舷梯組成了一道密不透風的人牆。\n\n然而，在距離舷梯不到二十米的跑道中央，一道纖細的身影卻如同一株扎根在水泥地裡的修竹，孤身一人擋住了登機通道。\n\n蘇棠身上依然套著市局技術科的深藍色執勤夾克，懷裡抱著那台加固軍用筆記型電腦，指尖在鍵盤上急速翻飛。\n\n「小姑娘，你以為憑你一個人，一台中學生一樣的筆記本，就能攔住我宋懷德？」宋懷德吐出一口青藍色的雪茄煙霧，眼角堆滿了上位者居高臨下的冷酷與譏誚，「三十年前你父親林清源拿著整箱的化驗單試圖告倒我，結果他的骨頭現在還在江底餵魚。你今天站在這裡，除了替他送命，沒有任何意義。」\n\n「我不是來攔你的。」蘇棠抬起頭，眼眶通紅，但那雙清澈的眸子裡卻燃燒著如烈日般決絕的怒火，「我是來為全濱江的死者，送你最後一程。」\n\n「啪！」\n\n蘇棠重重按下了回車鍵！\n\n就在這一微秒之間，整個濱江國際機場航站樓、貴賓候機廳、塔台指揮中心以及全市數千塊戶外LED大螢幕上，原本滾動的航班資訊與商業廣告瞬間被強制切斷！\n\n取而代之的，是林清源三十年前那份蓋著絕密鋼印的病理報告原稿，以及宋懷德當年收受三百二十萬美元海外匯款的全部存根照片！\n\n與此同時，機場廣播系統中，突然響起了三十年前林清源生前留下的最後一段清晰錄音：\n\n『……抗癌多肽製劑9407批次存在致命骨髓基因毒性，五至十年內致死率高達百分之八十！我身為病理醫生，絕不在這份批准文號上簽字！宋懷德，你就算把長江的水抽乾，也洗不淨你手上的血！』\n\n整個國際機場瞬間陷入了死一般的震撼！\n\n宋懷德臉上的從容優雅在這一瞬間徹底粉碎，臉色慘白如死灰。\n\n「殺了她！把電腦給我砸碎！」宋懷德氣急敗壞地指著蘇棠尖叫。\n\n三名境外保鏢瞬間拔出裝有消音器的自動手槍，黑洞洞的槍口直指蘇棠的眉心！\n\n就在擊針即將撞擊底火的千鈞一髮之際——\n\n「轟————！！」\n\n一聲猶如狂暴公牛般的引擎咆哮自停機坪防護欄外驟然炸響！\n\n只見那輛滿身泥濘、保險槓早已撞凹的老桑塔納警車，以時速一百二十公里的極限速度撞碎了跑道鐵絲網，在水泥路面上拉出四道刺鼻的黑色胎印，如同一面鋼鐵盾牌般一個漂移橫甩，生生橫亙在蘇棠與槍口之間！\n\n「砰！砰！砰！」\n\n三顆子彈擦著桑塔納的防爆鋼板濺起耀眼的火花！\n\n「市局刑偵支隊！所有人放下武器！！」老周雙手持槍從車門後探出身軀，眼神兇悍得像一頭被徹底激怒的老獅子。\n\n「垂死掙扎！」宋懷德眼中閃過一抹癲狂，一把推開身前的保鏢，左手猛然從大衣口袋裡掏出一柄極其小巧的純金袖珍手槍，獰笑著直撲舷梯，「只要飛機滑行起飛，你們這群臭警察能奈我何？！」\n\n就在宋懷德右腳踏上舷梯第一級台階的瞬間——\n\n「嗖！」\n\n一道凌厲刺目的銀芒撕裂清晨的薄霧，劃出一道超越人體視覺極限的筆直銀線！\n\n那是一柄純銀打造的十四號解剖手術刀！\n\n手術刀在半空中精準旋轉了整整三圈，鋒利冰冷的刀尖帶著破空的銳響，「奪」的一聲，毫釐不差地刺穿了宋懷德的右手掌骨邊緣，將他手中的金槍連同隨身保險箱的提手，死死釘在了舷梯堅硬的鋁合金扶手上！\n\n「啊————！！」\n\n宋懷德發出一聲殺豬般的慘嚎，鮮血順著刀刃瘋狂滴落。\n\n裴以安雙手插在大衣口袋裡，腳踩著被晨霧打濕的跑道，緩緩從警車後方邁步走出。金絲眼鏡後的目光清澈冷冽，宛如在巡視一座早已蓋棺定論的解剖台。\n\n「右側第二掌骨淺表穿透傷，未傷及橈動脈與尺神經。」裴以安的聲音沒有一絲溫度，「精確控制出血量在十毫升以內，完全符合正當防衛與制服嫌疑人的法醫力學標準。」\n\n「小畜生……你找死！」宋懷德疼得滿頭大汗，面容扭曲地揚起戴著那枚重金印章戒指的左拳，用盡全身力量朝著裴以安的面門狠狠砸去！\n\n那是三十年前，在二號乾塢擊碎林清源枕骨的致命鐵拳！\n\n然而，裴以安甚至連眉毛都沒有抬一下。\n\n就在鐵拳距離鼻尖僅剩三公分的剎那，裴以安修長的手掌如靈蛇出洞般精準探出，五指如鋼箍般卡住了宋懷德的左手腕橈橈骨莖突！\n\n反關節扣鎖！\n\n「喀嚓！」\n\n伴隨著一聲清脆的脫臼聲，宋懷德的整條左臂被瞬間反剪在身後，整個人撲通一聲被生生按跪在冰冷潮濕的水泥地上！\n\n裴以安用一把止血鉗夾住宋懷德左手食指上的那枚黃金印章戒指，手腕發力，輕輕一旋。\n\n沾滿冷汗的戒指被完整剝離。\n\n「純金打造，內徑二十二毫米，外緣帶有省醫學會理事徽章的微型鋸齒狀花紋。」裴以安居高臨下地俯視著跪在地上的前副市長，將戒指舉在朝陽之下，「三十年前，你在林清源博士枕骨大孔左側留下的凹痕，尺寸剛好是四毫米乘七毫米。」\n\n「宋懷德，三十年前你用這枚戒指在骨頭上寫下了謀殺的罪證；今天，這枚戒指將親手把你送上審判席。」\n\n跑道遠處，十幾輛閃爍著警燈的特警裝甲車與反恐突擊車呼嘯而至，將整個灣流商務機團團圍死。民航局的地面指揮車更是直接封鎖了滑行跑道，宋懷德的外逃之路被彻底截斷！\n\n老周邁著沉重的步伐走上前，將一副沉甸甸的警用鋼銬重重銬在宋懷德的手腕上。\n\n「宋副市長，三十年前你從林博士手裡奪走的，今天該一分不差地吐出來了。」老周冷冷吐出一口唾沫。\n\n舷梯旁，蘇棠雙手緊緊抱著膝蓋，淚水終於決堤般奪眶而出，失聲痛哭。\n\n三十年的流離失所，三十年的冤屈與黑暗，在這一刻被晨光徹底滌蕩乾淨。\n\n老周走上前，脫下自己那件寬大的灰色抓絨警服，輕輕披在女孩單薄的肩膀上。隨後，他從防彈背心裡掏出那隻立下奇功的粉紅色保溫杯，擰開蓋子，遞到了蘇棠面前。\n\n「丫頭……口渴了吧？喝口老周特供的大紅袍。」老周臉上的皺紋舒展開來，笑得無比溫柔，「三十年了……你爸的案子，咱們破了。」\n\n蘇棠雙手捧著溫暖的保溫杯，看著熱騰騰的白霧升騰而起，用力地點了點頭。\n\n晨霧散盡，一輪璀璨的紅日自長江江面噴薄而出，將整座濱江市染成一片耀眼的燦爛金紅。\n\n裴以安拔出釘在舷梯上的十四號手術刀，用一塊無菌紗布擦淨刀刃上的血跡，抬眼望向東方那片明朗的天空。\n\n死者已無遺憾，人間再無冤魂。\n\n【全書終局倒數 · 第十九章完】","rawContentEn":"# Chapter 19: The Final Scalpel Piercing the Mist\n\nAt 7:15 in the morning, West Apron Private Aviation Terminal, Binjiang International Airport.\n\nMorning fog drifted like a white gossamer veil across the sprawling tarmac, where a silver-gray Gulfstream G650 screamed with the deep, throaty rumble of twin turbofans, its tail nozzles billowing visible heat mirages during final pre-flight checks.\n\nAt the foot of the airstairs, seventy-year-old former Deputy Mayor Song Huaide stood draped in an impeccably tailored charcoal cashmere topcoat, a cigar balanced in his left hand while his right clamped onto a titanium security briefcase.\n\nFlanking his flanks, eight overseas private security contractors clad in dark suits and acoustic earpieces rested their palms upon underarm holsters, forming an impenetrable human shield against the ladder.\n\nYet less than twenty meters away in the dead center of the apron, a slender silhouette stood rooted like bamboo into the reinforced concrete, barring the boarding lane entirely alone.\n\nSu Tang remained dressed in her navy technical duty jacket, cradling her ruggedized military laptop as her fingers flew across the keyboard in a dazzling blur.\n\n\"Little girl, do you truly imagine that by standing alone with a toy laptop, you can obstruct Song Huaide?\" Song Huaide exhaled a coil of blue cigar smoke, his crow's feet creasing with the imperious malice of entrenched power. \"Thirty years ago, your father Lin Qingyuan brandished crates of lab assays attempting to bring me down; today, his bones are still feeding river fish. Standing here accomplishes nothing beyond throwing your life away after his.\"\n\n\"I am not here to block your path,\" Su Tang raised her head, eyes bloodshot yet blazing with a righteous, incandescent fury like the noon sun. \"I am here on behalf of all the dead of Binjiang—to see you to your final reckoning.\"\n\nClack!\n\nSu Tang hammered the return key with resolute force!\n\nIn that fractional microsecond, across all terminal concourses, VIP departure lounges, air traffic control towers, and thousands of municipal outdoor LED billboards, all rolling flight manifests and commercial broadcasts were hijacked simultaneously!\n\nIn their place blazed Lin Qingyuan's original 1994 pathology manuscript bearing its top-secret institutional stamps, flanked by high-resolution scans of the wire transfer vouchers detailing Song Huaide's $3.2 million overseas bribery windfall!\n\nConcurrently, through the airport's master public address system roared the final surviving voice recording left by Dr. Lin Qingyuan thirty years ago:\n\n\"The anti-neoplastic biologic Batch 9407 carries catastrophic genetic myelotoxicity—its five-to-ten-year mortality exceeds eighty percent! As a physician of pathology, I will never append my signature to this authorization! Song Huaide, you could pump the Yangtze River dry and never wash the blood from your hands!\"\n\nThe entire international aerodrome fell into stunned, breathless petrification!\n\nThe veneer of aristocratic composure shattered from Song Huaide's visage, turning him ashen as a corpse.\n\n\"Kill her! Smash that machine to atoms!\" Song Huaide shrieked, stabbing a trembling finger toward Su Tang.\n\nThree contractors drew suppressed automatic pistols in unison, black muzzles centering squarely upon Su Tang's forehead!\n\nIn the breathless heartbeat before firing pins struck primers—\n\nROARRRRR——!!\n\nThe furious roar of an engine charged like an enraged bull, shattering the security perimeter fence!\n\nSpewing mud and sporting a crumpled bumper, the aged Santana cruiser burst through the chain-link barrier at 120 kilometers per hour, laying down four smoking ribbons of scorched rubber as it executed a tactical drift, interposing its steel hull as an armored barricade between Su Tang and the gunfire!\n\nCrack! Crack! Crack!\n\nThree hollow-points ricocheted off the door plating, spitting brilliant sparks of fire!\n\n\"Police! Criminal Investigation Detachment! Drop your weapons!!\" Old Zhou leaned out from behind the reinforced doorframe with his service weapon, his eyes as fierce as an enraged lion.\n\n\"Pathetic dying kicks!\" Madness flared in Song Huaide's pupils as he shoved past his mercenaries, yanking a miniature solid-gold derringer from his coat and lunging toward the airstairs with a feral grin. \"Once my jet rolls down the runway, what can you worthless flatfoots do to touch me?!\"\n\nThe instant Song Huaide's boot touched the first tread of the ladder—\n\nSHING!\n\nA blinding streak of silver ripped through the morning mist, drawing a trajectory that defied human visual reflex!\n\nIt was a solid-silver No. 14 dissecting scalpel!\n\nRevolving three times with mathematical symmetry, the razor-honed blade struck home with a concussive thud, pinning the margin of Song Huaide's right metacarpal alongside the briefcase handle dead into the solid aluminum handrail!\n\n\"AAARRRGGGHHH——!!\"\n\nSong Huaide howled like a slaughtered beast as arterial blood cascaded down the blade.\n\nHands tucked into his coat pockets, Pei Yi'an paced across the dewy apron from behind the cruiser, his gaze behind rimless spectacles as tranquil and cold as a pathologist surveying a post-mortem table.\n\n\"Superficial transfixion of the right second metacarpal margin, sparing both radial artery and ulnar nerve bundles,\" Pei Yi'an noted with surgical detachment. \"Blood loss strictly regulated below ten milliliters, fully conforming to forensic biomechanical standards for suspect immobilization.\"\n\n\"You insolent whelp... I'll crush you!\" Sweating profusely in agony, Song Huaide swung his left fist bearing the heavy gold signet ring, throwing every ounce of his weight directly at Pei Yi'an's face!\n\nIt was the exact lethal blow that had caved in Lin Qingyuan's skull at Dry Dock No. 2 thirty years ago!\n\nPei Yi'an did not so much as twitch a brow.\n\nThree centimeters from his spectacles, Pei Yi'an's hand snapped forward like striking viper, fingers clamping like a steel vise over Song Huaide's radial styloid process!\n\nJoint reversal lock!\n\nCRACK!\n\nWith a sharp subluxation snap, Song Huaide's left arm was twisted behind his spine, forcing the former statesman to his knees upon the icy tarmac with an undignified splash!\n\nEmploying hemostatic forceps, Pei Yi'an clamped the golden signet ring upon Song's index finger, executing a deft twist.\n\nThe sweat-slicked ring peeled cleanly from the flesh.\n\n\"Solid gold alloy, inner bore twenty-two millimeters, its outer rim inscribed with the serrated crest of the Provincial Medical Council,\" Pei Yi'an hoisted the artifact into the morning glare, looking down upon the fallen dignitary. \"Thirty years ago, the dent you stamped into the bone beside Dr. Lin Qingyuan's foramen magnum measured precisely four millimeters by seven.\"\n\n\"Song Huaide, thirty years ago you etched your confession upon human bone with this ring; today, this very token escorts you straight to the prisoner's dock.\"\n\nIn the near distance, a dozen SWAT armored carriers and tactical assault vans arrived in deafening thunder, hemming the Gulfstream within an impenetrable cordon. Ground controllers blocked the taxiway—Song Huaide's escape was extinguished forever!\n\nStiding forward with heavy, deliberate tread, Old Zhou slammed heavy steel handcuffs around Song Huaide's wrists.\n\n\"Deputy Mayor Song, everything you stole from Dr. Lin thirty years ago—today you cough back up to the very last cent,\" Old Zhou spat contemptuously onto the asphalt.\n\nBy the airstairs, Su Tang pulled her knees to her chest, the dam collapsing as tears poured unchecked down her cheeks in ragged sobs.\n\nThirty years of displacement, thirty years of stifling darkness, washed pure in this singular bath of dawn.\n\nWalking over, Old Zhou unzipped his oversized gray fleece jacket, gently draping it over the young woman's trembling shoulders. From within his tactical vest, he drew forth his legendary pink thermos, unscrewing the cap and offering it forward.\n\n\"Little girl... you must be parched. Have some of Old Zhou's private-reserve Da Hong Pao,\" the wrinkles across the veteran detective's brow relaxed into tender warmth. \"Thirty years... Your father's case is solved.\"\n\nCupping the warm flask with both hands as aromatic steam curled upward, Su Tang nodded with all her might.\n\nThe morning mist vanished entirely. A blazing sun crested the rolling currents of the Yangtze, gilding the skyline of Binjiang in triumphant scarlet and gold.\n\nWrenching the No. 14 scalpel from the aluminum ladder, Pei Yi'an cleansed the steel with sterile gauze, gazing upward into the immaculate eastern heavens.\n\nThe departed harbored no remaining regret; beneath the heavens, no restless ghost lingered in silence.\n\n[Grand Finale Countdown · End of Chapter 19]"},{"id":20,"rawContent":"# 第二十章：黎明時分，死者請安息\n\n一個月後，深秋的清晨。\n\n滾滾長江自濱江市中心穿城而過，江面上的薄霧在初升朝陽的照耀下泛著溫柔的金紅色波光。\n\n濱江市中級人民法院第一審判庭的大門外，數百名各大媒體的記者與市民正屏息注視著大螢幕上的即時宣判直播。\n\n被告人席上，身穿囚服、面容枯槁的宋懷德與楚天成垂著頭，聽著法槌重重落下的清脆巨響。\n\n跨越三十年的特大貪腐、故意殺人、偽造國家醫藥審批案塵埃落定。宋懷德被判處死刑，楚天成被判處無期徒刑，涉案的二十三名原衛生系統腐敗官員無一漏網。\n\n而在證人席上，完成了人生最後一場證言的顧志明，在兩名檢察官的攙扶下緩緩站起身。老人仰頭看著法庭正上方莊嚴的國徽，臉上終於露出了三十年來未曾有過的一抹釋然笑容。他在一週後平靜離世，臨終前將自己所有的醫學遺產與專利分紅，全部捐贈給了濱江市法醫病理青年科研基金。\n\n涉案的秦墨因重大立功表現且長期受到精神脅迫，被依法免於死刑，送往專門醫療機構接受封閉式心理康復治療。\n\n此時此刻，濱江市南山烈士陵園最頂層的松柏林中，微風吹拂著潔白的石階。\n\n一座嶄新的漢白玉合葬墓碑前，擺滿了清香四溢的白菊。\n\n墓碑上鐫刻著兩個並排的名字：**林清源**、**陳衛國**。\n\n在墓碑前的石台正中央，端正擺放著一份剛剛由市局蓋章生效的特殊文件——**【一九九四年七月十七日二號乾塢特大命案·終審法醫學鑒定書】**。\n\n鑒定結論那一欄，用蒼勁俐落的鋼筆字工整書寫著四個字：**【機械性鈍器他殺】**。\n\n簽發法醫那一欄，赫然簽署著三個清秀剛勁的字跡：**裴以安**。\n\n身著深藍色常服警服的蘇棠站在墓碑前，向著父親深深鞠了三個躬，眼角泛著晶瑩的淚光，但嘴角卻揚起了一抹陽光般溫暖的弧度。\n\n「爸，陳叔叔，」蘇棠輕聲呢喃，指尖拂過冰涼的墓碑，「你們的名字，乾乾淨淨地回來了。」\n\n老周身穿筆挺的警禮服，胸前掛著嶄新的二等功獎章，抬起右手，向著墓碑敬了一個標準無比的警禮。\n\n裴以安一言不發，將一束純白色的洋桔梗輕輕放在墓碑前，隨後退後半步，微微頷首。\n\n死者已昭雪，人間復清明。\n\n……\n\n當天深夜，老城區濱江路那間熟悉的大排檔。\n\n紅泥小爐上的砂鍋正咕嘟咕嘟冒著滾燙的白氣，空氣中瀰漫著牛雜、老薑與陳年紹興花雕的濃郁香氣。\n\n老周早已脫下了拘束的禮服，換上了那件洗得泛白的舊夾克，心滿意足地吸溜了一大口熱騰騰的粉絲牛雜湯。\n\n在他的手邊，那隻褪色的粉紅色保溫杯依然穩穩立在摺疊桌中央。\n\n只不過，保溫杯的杯蓋側面，此時竟多出了一枚由市局警務保障處特製的迷你鍍銀銘牌：**【市局一等功功勳保溫杯·承重四百五十克】**。\n\n「哎呀，舒坦！」老周抹了一把油汪汪的嘴巴，拍著肚子靠在塑料靠背椅上，滿臉得意地指著保溫杯，「小裴，你看，老陸這回辦事總算厚道了一回。連局長都承認，要是沒有老子這半杯大紅袍的配重，你現在就得在烈士陵園裡跟我做鄰居！」\n\n坐在對面的裴以安穿著乾淨的黑色風衣，正用一柄隨身攜帶的銀色小鑷子，極其精準地將湯碗裡的香菜葉一片片挑出來。\n\n「從力學與熱力學角度考量，你當時能夠生還，百分之九十九點九依賴於那座防空地堡通風管道的逆向壓力釋放閥。」裴以安頭也不抬，神色冷淡地糾正，「你的保溫杯只是剛好充當了零點四五公斤的物理重塊。換成一塊同等重量的煤渣，效果完全一致。」\n\n「你小子，一天不拆老子的台你能少塊肉是不是？」老周翻了個白眼，抓起保溫杯美滋滋地灌了一口溫水，「下個月老子就滿五十五了，老陸問我想不想退居二線去警校當個榮譽教官。我尋思著，也是時候退休釣釣魚、養養花，省得天天半夜被你拽去停屍房聞福馬林。」\n\n裴以安停下手中的鑷子，金絲眼鏡後的目光平靜地抬起，看著老周那張寫滿滄桑卻神采奕奕的老臉。\n\n「根據市局最新公佈的警務骨幹延聘條例，具備高級技術職稱與三十年現場勘查經驗的資深刑警，延遲退休申請通常具備最高優先審批權。」裴以安將一碟剛出鍋的生煎包推到老周面前，「老周，你的公傷申請我已經替你寫好了。病假批了三天，下週一早上八點，實驗室見。」\n\n老周愣了愣，低頭看著那碟金黃焦脆的生煎包，眼角忍不住泛起一抹笑意，嘴裡卻笑罵道：\n\n「沒大沒小的臭小子……你連老子的退休生活都要給解剖了？」\n\n就在這時，老周腰間那台剛剛換了新電池的警用對講機，突然毫無預兆地發出了一陣急促刺耳的電波呼叫聲：\n\n「呼叫周成林！呼叫裴以安法醫！」\n\n「濱江港四號老碼頭剛剛打撈上來一隻被鐵鏈重重纏繞的沉睡鐵箱，箱體表面殘留著大量年代久遠的特殊封蠟印記！」\n\n「現場民警請求法醫病理專家與重案組立即支援！」\n\n大排檔的夜風吹拂著兩人的衣擺。\n\n老周與裴以安對視了一眼。\n\n老刑警無奈地長嘆了一口氣，伸手擰緊了那隻粉紅色保溫杯的杯蓋，隨後利落地拔出轉椅旁的配槍檢查彈匣，嘴角揚起一抹銳利而熟悉的笑容：\n\n「得，小裴，看來這座城市裡的死人，今晚又不想讓我們安生睡覺了。」\n\n裴以安緩緩站起身，扣上黑色風衣的排扣，骨節分明的右手穩穩提起那隻反射著晨星微光的銀色勘查箱。\n\n他的眼神冷冽如初，嘴角卻在夜色中勾起了一抹極淡、極從容的弧度：\n\n「死者比活人更有禮貌。」\n\n「走吧，周隊——去讓他們保持安靜。」\n\n【全書完 · 圓滿大結局】","rawContentEn":"# Chapter 20: At Dawn, May the Dead Rest in Peace\n\nOne month later, a crisp morning in late autumn.\n\nThe rolling Yangtze River cleaved through the heart of Binjiang, its morning mist shimmering with gentle ripples of gold and rose beneath the nascent sun.\n\nOutside the grand bronze doors of Courtroom No. 1 at the Binjiang Intermediate People's Court, hundreds of journalists and citizens held their collective breath, watching the live sentencing verdict broadcast across outdoor monitors.\n\nIn the dock, clad in prison garb and hollow-cheeked, Song Huaide and Chu Tiancheng hung their heads as the sharp crack of the judicial gavel resounded like a thunderclap.\n\nSpanning three decades of grand corruption, intentional homicide, and forged national pharmaceutical authorizations, the gavel fell on the conspiracy. Song Huaide was sentenced to capital punishment, Chu Tiancheng to life imprisonment, and not a single one of the twenty-three corrupt medical bureaucrats escaped the net of justice.\n\nIn the witness box, having delivered his final earthly testimony, Gu Zhiming rose slowly supported by two bailiffs. Gazing upward at the solemn national emblem, a serene smile graced the old pathologist's lips for the first time in thirty years. He passed away peacefully one week later, leaving his entire estate and patent royalties to establish the Binjiang Forensic Pathology Youth Research Endowment.\n\nQin Mo, recognized for substantial mitigating cooperation and long-term psychological duress, was spared capital punishment under statute and committed to a specialized forensic medical facility for inpatient rehabilitation.\n\nAt this moment, amidst the evergreen pines atop Binjiang's Nanshan Cemetery, a mild breeze brushed the white stone stairs.\n\nBefore a newly erected cenotaph of white marble lay armfuls of fragrant white chrysanthemums.\n\nEngraved side by side upon the headstone were two names: **Lin Qingyuan** and **Chen Weiguo**.\n\nResting in the center of the granite plinth was an official dossier just validated by Bureau seals—**[Final Forensic Post-Mortem Certificate: The Homicide of July 17, 1994, at Dry Dock No. 2]**.\n\nUnder the finding of cause of death was inscribed in sharp, elegant ink four decisive words: **[Blunt-Force Traumatic Homicide]**.\n\nAnd in the examiner's signature box stood three clean, incisive characters: **Pei Yi'an**.\n\nDressed in her navy police service uniform, Su Tang bowed three times before her father's monument, tears glistening at her lashes while a warm, radiant smile curled upon her lips.\n\n\"Dad, Uncle Chen,\" Su Tang whispered, her fingertips caressing the cool marble. \"Your names have returned to the light—pure and unblemished.\"\n\nStanding straight in his ceremonial tunic, a gleaming Second-Class Merit Star pinned to his lapel, Old Zhou snapped an immaculate, rigid salute toward the monument.\n\nUttering no words, Pei Yi'an placed a sprig of white lisianthus gently upon the dais, stepping back half a pace and offering a solemn bow.\n\nThe departed had been vindicated; clarity returned to the world of the living.\n\n...\n\nLate that night, at the familiar roadside food stall along Binjiang Road in the old quarter.\n\nThe clay pot atop the charcoal brazier bubbled merrily with steaming broth, filling the chilly night air with the rich aroma of braised tripe, aged ginger, and Shaoxing rice wine.\n\nHaving shed his stifling dress uniform for his faded, beloved casual jacket, Old Zhou slurped a hearty mouthful of hot vermicelli and ox offal with profound contentment.\n\nAt his elbow, the battered pink thermos stood proudly in the middle of the folding table.\n\nOnly now, affixed to the lid was a miniature silver-plated citation plaque custom-crafted by the Bureau's Logistics Department: **[Bureau First-Class Meritorious Thermos · Calibrated Mass: 450 Grams]**.\n\n\"Ah, pure bliss!\" Old Zhou wiped his glistening lips, patting his stomach as he reclined in the plastic chair, pointing smugly at the flask. \"Little Pei, look at that—Chief Lu actually did right by me for once! Even the Commissioner admitted that without the counterweight of my half-cup of Da Hong Pao, you'd be bunking as my neighbor up on the martyr's hill right now!\"\n\nSeated opposite him in an immaculate black trench coat, Pei Yi'an wielded a small pair of pocket silver forceps, systematically and surgically plucking every solitary coriander leaf from his soup bowl.\n\n\"Evaluating from mechanical and thermodynamic principles, your survival was 99.9% attributable to the reverse pressure-relief actuators of the bunker ventilation shaft,\" Pei Yi'an corrected dispassionately without lifting his eyes. \"Your thermos merely served as an arbitrary 0.45-kilogram mass. Had we placed a lump of coal of identical heft upon the pan, the outcome would have been identical.\"\n\n\"You little brat, would it kill you to let me have my moment for once?\" Old Zhou rolled his eyes, unscrewing his cap to take a satisfied gulp of warm tea. \"I turn fifty-five next month. Chief Lu asked if I wanted to transition to the Police Academy as an honorary instructor. I figure it's time to take up fishing and tend some orchids, so I don't get dragged into the morgue at 3:00 AM to sniff formalin every night.\"\n\nPei Yi'an paused his forceps, his eyes behind gold rims lifting quietly to regard Old Zhou's weathered, yet thoroughly rejuvenated countenance.\n\n\"Pursuant to the Department's latest veteran retention directives, senior investigators commanding master technical credentials and thirty years of crime scene experience receive expedited approval for delayed retirement,\" Pei Yi'an pushed a plate of piping-hot pan-fried buns across the table. \"Captain Zhou, I took the liberty of filing your workman's compensation report. You are granted three days of sick leave. Monday at 8:00 AM sharp—see you in the lab.\"\n\nOld Zhou froze, looking down at the crispy golden dumplings, a grin tugging at the corners of his mouth despite his grumbling retort:\n\n\"Cheeky little imp... Are you dissecting my retirement plans now too?\"\n\nJust then, the radio on Old Zhou's duty belt—freshly fitted with new batteries—chirped with an urgent tactical alert:\n\n\"Dispatch to Captain Zhou Chenglin! Urgent dispatch to Pathologist Pei Yi'an!\"\n\n\"River Patrol just salvaged an iron steamer trunk bound in heavy mooring chains off Pier No. 4! The casing bears extensive, antique wax seals!\"\n\n\"On-scene officers request immediate technical forensic and Major Crimes backup!\"\n\nThe night breeze of the riverside stall ruffled their coats.\n\nOld Zhou and Pei Yi'an locked eyes across the table.\n\nExhaling a helpless, fond sigh, the veteran detective cranked the lid of his pink thermos tight, snapped his service pistol back into his holster, and flashed his signature, battle-hardened grin:\n\n\"Well, Little Pei, seems the dead in Binjiang aren't in the mood to let us get a full night's sleep after all.\"\n\nRising in measured grace, Pei Yi'an buttoned his trench coat, his slender fingers gripping the handle of the silver field kit gleaming under the starlight.\n\nHis gaze remained as cool as winter frost, yet in the shadows of the night, his lips curved into an imperceptible, confident smile:\n\n\"The dead are far more polite than the living.\"\n\n\"Let us move, Captain Zhou—and help them keep their peace.\"\n\n[The End · Grand Finale]"}];
